WEBVTT


00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.430
Where have you been?
I've been waiting since 7:00.


00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.867
Get in. I had to find fireworks.


00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.164
Let me drive.


00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.536
Get in. I haven't eaten in 24 hours.


00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.068
Are you coming or not?


00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.899
It's too crowded.


00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.798
I thought you were starving.


00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.766
Let's go someplace quiet.


00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.469
Okay.


00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.682
What are we doing?


00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.589
Sitting. Listening to music. Talking.


00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.497
- You seem weird. Is everything okay?
- Yeah, everything's fine.


00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.071
It's July.
How many shirts are you wearing?


00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:28.272
- I'm cold.
- You're cold on the Fourth of July?


00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.811
Fuck off and die!


00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:44.255
- What?
- "Fuck off and die"?


00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.093
Shut up.


00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.652
Was that car at the drive-in?


00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.323
I saw that car at Mr. Ed's.


00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:29.003
- Do you want me to tell him to leave?
- Stay in the car.


00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.416
- Was that your husband?
- No.


00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.528
Who was that, Darlene?


00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.559
Don't worry about it.


00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.104
- Don't tell me not to worry. Who was it?
- It's nothing.


00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.281
Oh, shit.


00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.891
Let's go.


00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.662
Now, D.


00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.471
Get your wallet.


00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.026
Man, you really creeped us out.


00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:59.318
<i>- Vallejo Police Department.
- I want to report a double murder.</i>


00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.017
<i>May I have your name
and where you are calling...</i>


00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.493
<i>If you go one mile east
on Columbus Parkway,</i>


00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.827
<i>a public park,
you'll find kids in a brown car.</i>


00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.564
<i>They were shot with a 9mm Luger.</i>


00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.732
<i>I also killed those kids last year.</i>


00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.933
<i>Goodbye.</i>


00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:35.985
Spit.


00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.593
Come on, buddy.


00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:41.667
- I swallowed it.
- Why?


00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.133
It was minty.


00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.638
You can't do that. It's not good for you.


00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.040
Lunch box.


00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:52.077
- Why am I not going on the bus?
- Because we're late.


00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:57.379
Okay, you're staying
with your mom and Aaron tonight.


00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.212
So, you don't like
having a new little brother?


00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.652
- No, not really.
- Oh, that's honest.


00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:07.652
Learn a lot.


00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.728
There will be a test tonight!


00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.092
Morning.


00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.469
- Morning.
- Morning.


00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.423
How's the coffee today, Shorty?


00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.534
Editorial in two.


00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.666
Good morning, gentlemen.


00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:37.003
- Good morning.
- Good morning.


00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.043
Well, Stanton, tell Mr. Howe


00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.636
the draft board piece
was damn near perfect.


00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.315
Mr. Graysmith.


00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:47.250
Horrid.


00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.411
Horrid.


00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:50.716
Not so horrid.


00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:53.587
All right.
I'm thinking we go with not so horrid.


00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:58.957
Paul, what's on the crime beat?


00:09:59.065 --> 00:10:03.195
Janice in Datebook left the fondue party
before everyone got naked.


00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:04.599
That's a crime.


00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:07.229
Have you seen her? Wouldn't kid you.


00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.706
It may be the beginning of a crime wave.


00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.441
You need to see this.


00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.681
Go get the publisher.


00:10:19.785 --> 00:10:20.877
"Dear Editor,


00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:22.045
"This is the murderer


00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:24.349
"of the two teenagers
last Christmas at Lake Herman


00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:27.483
"and the girl on the Fourth of July
near the golf course in Vallejo.


00:10:27.593 --> 00:10:28.992
"To prove I killed them,


00:10:29.095 --> 00:10:32.462
"I shall state some facts
which only I and the police know.


00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:35.898
"Christmas,
brand name of ammo, Super-X.


00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:38.269
"Ten shots were fired.


00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:41.169
"The boy was on his back
with his feet to the car.


00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.535
"The girl... "


00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:47.803
Would you read that, please?


00:10:49.048 --> 00:10:51.539
"The girl was on her right side,
feet to the west.


00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:53.312
"Fourth of July.


00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:56.286
"One, girl was
wearing patterned slacks.


00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:58.448
"The boy was also shot in the knee.


00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:00.889
"Brand name of ammo was Western.


00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:03.357
"Here is part of a cipher.


00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:06.954
"The other two parts of this cipher
are being mailed to the editors of


00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:09.899
<i>"the Vallejo Times and S.F. Examiner.</i>


00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:13.802
"I want you to print this cipher
on the front page of your paper.


00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:16.306
"In this cipher is my identity.


00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:18.900
"If you do not print this cipher
by the afternoon of Fry,"


00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:25.007
F- R-Y, "First of Aug '69
I will go on a kill rampage Fry night.


00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:29.417
"I will cruise around all weekend
killing lone people in the night


00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:31.046
"then move on to kill again


00:11:31.157 --> 00:11:34.786
"until I end up with
a dozen people over the weekend. "


00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:36.987
It's unsigned except for a symbol.


00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:41.826
Is it me,
or does that look like a gunsight?


00:11:43.302 --> 00:11:45.167
Today's August first.


00:11:45.271 --> 00:11:46.898
He wants his code
in the afternoon edition.


00:11:47.006 --> 00:11:49.702
<i>If the Examiner doesn't have
the balls to run it, we scoop the Bay.</i>


00:11:49.809 --> 00:11:51.868
Al, this man is talking about
shooting 12 people.


00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:53.774
And not running this
might make him do that.


00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.347
If we run it, we might be setting
a very dangerous precedent.


00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:58.076
Oh, come on, now, it's newsworthy.


00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:00.209
Well, giving some sick bastard
a soapbox,


00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.343
what does that say to people?


00:12:01.454 --> 00:12:04.651
Back up. Is this Vallejo story true?
Do we know that?


00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:07.726
- Paul?
- What? I cover crime in Vallejo?


00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:10.825
Yeah, I cover crime in Vallejo.
Ten minutes.


00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.262
Let's shoot the code and call SFPD.


00:12:13.365 --> 00:12:16.698
If it turns out to be real,
at least we'll have the material.


00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:18.830
All right.


00:12:19.772 --> 00:12:22.036
Graysmith,
don't you have that cartoon to finish?


00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:23.369
Oh, yeah.


00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:32.145
<i>Hi, this is Paul Avery
from the San Francisco Chronicle.</i>


00:12:32.251 --> 00:12:35.277
I'm looking for someone to
shed some light on a letter we received.


00:12:36.155 --> 00:12:37.179
Thank you.


00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.714
Sergeant Mulanax.


00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:40.587
<i>Sergeant, Paul Avery from
the San Francisco Chronicle.</i>


00:12:40.693 --> 00:12:41.717
I just wanted to check


00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:43.852
if you had an unsolved
firearm-related homicide


00:12:43.963 --> 00:12:46.625
on Christmas and
maybe one on July fourth.


00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:47.892
Shit.


00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:49.799
You guys got one, too?


00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.033
Confirmed.
VPD, they confirmed the shootings.


00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.198
<i>Al's on the phone with the Examiner.</i>


00:12:55.307 --> 00:12:56.706
They got the same letter
with a different code.


00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:57.867
<i>So did Times-Herald.</i>


00:12:57.977 --> 00:13:00.309
Christmas, two teenagers
on lover's lane. Both DOA.


00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:02.038
David Faraday and Betty Jensen.


00:13:02.148 --> 00:13:04.708
July fourth,
Darlene Ferrin and Michael...


00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:06.682
I think it's "Mayhew. "
Anyway, he lived, she didn't.


00:13:06.786 --> 00:13:07.844
The murder weapons?


00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:10.854
Ballistics, everything he said
in the letters matched.


00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:14.016
<i>I mean, I think the Times-Herald's
gonna go with it.</i>


00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:16.993
<i>The Examiner's going,
but won't go front page.</i>


00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:21.294
I say let's go front page.
If he kills 12 people, it's not our fault.


00:13:21.867 --> 00:13:24.427
Robert! We need the cartoon.


00:13:26.338 --> 00:13:29.501
- You're not finished?
- No, I'm finished, Carol. I'm finished.


00:13:29.608 --> 00:13:31.303
Thieriot's still here.


00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.570
Really?


00:13:33.045 --> 00:13:36.173
The first edition
is off the floor in 10, Charles.


00:13:39.552 --> 00:13:41.019
Give us a sec.


00:13:44.123 --> 00:13:45.613
Okay, re-plate.


00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:48.683
We'll go on page four.


00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:53.696
What do you say, 20 bucks
whoever cracks the psycho's name?


00:13:53.799 --> 00:13:55.664
He won't give his name.


00:13:56.936 --> 00:13:58.665
Morti's? Anyone?


00:13:58.771 --> 00:14:01.001
- That's where I'm heading.
- All right.


00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:29.990
Put those on my desk. Turn on the light.


00:14:41.313 --> 00:14:42.837
Grab your book.


00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:47.910
Now go get your jammies on.


00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.088
<i>All right, people, listen up.</i>


00:14:52.758 --> 00:14:57.627
The cipher's broken into three sections,
each with eight lines and 17 symbols.


00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.331
No breaks between the symbols
denoting different words.


00:15:00.432 --> 00:15:02.900
No numbers or clues
to substitution keys.


00:15:03.002 --> 00:15:05.493
And you got symbols
from at least seven different sources.


00:15:06.272 --> 00:15:11.107
Greek, Morse code, Navy semaphore,
weather symbols, astrological signs.


00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:20.045
- Hey, take a gander at this code thing.
- Okay.


00:15:25.391 --> 00:15:26.983
You wanna give it a go?


00:15:29.061 --> 00:15:32.030
Guy who used to sit there
was a great cartoonist. Bob Bastian.


00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:35.430
Now he's doing public television.
For some reason.


00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.367
Paul Avery.


00:15:39.838 --> 00:15:42.807
Robert Graysmith.
I've been here nine months.


00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:48.108
You were right, by the way.
He didn't give his name.


00:15:48.213 --> 00:15:49.271
Who cracked it?


00:15:49.381 --> 00:15:51.508
A history teacher
and his wife in Salinas.


00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:54.711
"I like killing people
because it is so much fun.


00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:58.847
"It is more fun
than killing wild game in the forest


00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:03.258
"because man is the most
dangerous animal of all to kill.


00:16:03.362 --> 00:16:06.263
"Something gives me
the most thrilling experience.


00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:10.324
"It is even better
than getting your rocks off with a girl.


00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:14.065
"The best part of it is that when I die,


00:16:14.173 --> 00:16:17.142
"I will be reborn in paradise.


00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:20.609
"And all that I have killed
will become my slaves.


00:16:20.713 --> 00:16:24.649
"I will not give you my name
because you will try to slow down


00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.776
"or stop my collecting of slaves
for my afterlife. "


00:16:27.886 --> 00:16:29.751
Methinks our friend's
a tad bit fuckered in the head.


00:16:29.855 --> 00:16:34.019
I heard he even sent Vallejo
a code key, just to help.


00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:36.492
- What is that at the bottom?
- Leftovers.


00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:38.187
Maybe an anagram.


00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.114
How does one do that?


00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.384
I like puzzles. I do them a lot.


00:17:01.487 --> 00:17:04.513
How did you know
he wasn't gonna give his name?


00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:06.717
Dangerous animal.


00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:09.185
Dangerous animal.


00:17:10.129 --> 00:17:12.996
What dangerous animal?
How do I know that?


00:17:20.372 --> 00:17:21.964
- Paul.
- Yes, Templeton.


00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:24.133
- Editorial, now.
- Very well.


00:17:26.311 --> 00:17:27.869
Another letter.


00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.279
More of the same.
Details about the murders.


00:17:32.418 --> 00:17:36.320
He taped a flashlight to the gun.
That's how he hit them in the dark.


00:17:36.422 --> 00:17:38.481
And he gave himself a name.


00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:02.739
You know this used to be
the town of Montecello?


00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:04.179
But at some point,


00:18:04.283 --> 00:18:07.446
the county decided that the land
would work better as a lake.


00:18:07.553 --> 00:18:09.248
So they flooded it.


00:18:10.722 --> 00:18:14.283
- But there's an entire...
- Hidden city under the water.


00:18:14.393 --> 00:18:16.691
We were here last spring, remember?


00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:18.194
Oh, yeah.


00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:26.134
Somebody else is here.


00:18:26.238 --> 00:18:27.967
It is a public park.


00:18:30.642 --> 00:18:32.735
I think he's watching us.


00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:35.006
Well, we're very good-looking.


00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:42.219
Where'd he go?


00:18:44.857 --> 00:18:46.620
He went behind that tree.


00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:49.091
All right. So he's taking a leak.


00:18:56.101 --> 00:18:57.966
He's coming towards us.


00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:01.940
Oh, my God, he has a gun.


00:19:02.841 --> 00:19:04.308
Don't move.


00:19:04.409 --> 00:19:07.276
- I want your money and your car keys.
- Okay.


00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.572
We're not gonna do anything, okay?


00:19:09.681 --> 00:19:13.173
We're gonna cooperate.
Just tell me what you want us to do.


00:19:17.055 --> 00:19:18.113
Here.


00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:22.983
You're welcome to everything I have.


00:19:26.565 --> 00:19:28.999
If there's anything else
I could do for you...


00:19:29.101 --> 00:19:31.399
Maybe I could write you a check?


00:19:33.972 --> 00:19:36.566
Okay, I could give you
my phone number.


00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:39.872
You know, I might be able to help you.


00:19:39.978 --> 00:19:42.071
Even more than you might think.


00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.240
He's a sociology major.


00:19:45.784 --> 00:19:48.378
Pre-law, actually.


00:19:50.522 --> 00:19:51.989
Oh, keys.


00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.217
You know, I'm sorry, I don't know exactly
where I put my keys.


00:19:54.326 --> 00:19:57.295
They might be on the blanket.
Is it okay if...


00:20:02.067 --> 00:20:03.625
Here's the keys.


00:20:05.103 --> 00:20:06.934
Don't get up.


00:20:07.039 --> 00:20:09.030
I want her to tie you up.


00:20:13.212 --> 00:20:14.304
Okay.


00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:37.092
You know, if he comes any closer,
I might be able to get that gun.


00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:39.397
- Don't get any ideas.
- I'm not.


00:20:39.504 --> 00:20:42.098
I killed a guard
escaping from prison in Montana.


00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.175
I'm not doing anything, okay?


00:20:44.276 --> 00:20:46.437
I'm not afraid to kill again.


00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.277
Look away.


00:20:56.521 --> 00:20:58.887
What was the name of that prison?


00:21:02.728 --> 00:21:05.288
Hey, you said it was in Montana, right?


00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:08.092
I'm taking your car.


00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.100
I'm going to Mexico.


00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:12.261
We didn't complain
when you tied our hands.


00:21:12.371 --> 00:21:14.339
Okay, you have everything that I have.


00:21:14.439 --> 00:21:17.272
We have done everything
that you've asked.


00:21:17.376 --> 00:21:18.707
It's okay. It's okay.


00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:21.074
She tied you loose, didn't she?


00:21:24.249 --> 00:21:26.342
Get on your stomach
so I can tie your feet.


00:21:26.451 --> 00:21:28.919
Okay.
It gets really cold out here at night.


00:21:29.021 --> 00:21:30.579
We could freeze.


00:21:38.997 --> 00:21:40.692
Okay, you all done?


00:21:42.734 --> 00:21:44.429
You know,
just because people are gonna ask,


00:21:44.536 --> 00:21:46.595
was that thing even loaded?


00:21:57.516 --> 00:21:59.484
It's okay.


00:21:59.584 --> 00:22:01.609
This is all gonna be okay.


00:22:30.649 --> 00:22:34.278
<i>Dispatch, this is 43L2,
heading south on Knoxville Road.</i>


00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:38.083
<i>I've got an abandoned white
VW Karmann-Ghia...</i>


00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.970
<i>Napa Police Department.</i>


00:22:54.072 --> 00:22:58.304
<i>I want to report a murder.
No, a double murder.</i>


00:22:59.845 --> 00:23:03.144
<i>They are two miles north
of park headquarters.</i>


00:23:03.248 --> 00:23:06.809
<i>They were in a white
Volkswagen Karmann-Ghia.</i>


00:23:08.387 --> 00:23:10.446
<i>I'm the one that did it.</i>


00:23:10.555 --> 00:23:12.614
<i>43L2 has a male victim with him.</i>


00:23:12.724 --> 00:23:15.318
<i>Piner's ambulance
has been dispatched.</i>


00:23:16.294 --> 00:23:18.455
Boy lived, the girl didn't. Again.


00:23:18.563 --> 00:23:20.929
God, can you imagine
surviving something like that?


00:23:21.032 --> 00:23:22.431
Writing the dates on the side of the car.


00:23:22.534 --> 00:23:25.628
We got two Vallejo killings,
now there's one in Napa. Why Napa?


00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:27.637
What the hell is he doing out of Vallejo?


00:23:27.739 --> 00:23:31.197
Sweet mother of Christ,
what are you drawing?


00:23:31.309 --> 00:23:32.799
Kid at the lake.


00:23:32.911 --> 00:23:34.708
This is what he said
the Zodiac was wearing.


00:23:34.813 --> 00:23:36.041
God, that's a hell of a get-up.


00:23:36.148 --> 00:23:38.582
- Paul, what are you doing?
- Hyman, I wrote it. It's done.


00:23:38.683 --> 00:23:39.911
Now I just got to type it up.


00:23:40.018 --> 00:23:41.986
Type it up?
It's not finished until you type it up.


00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:43.850
We've got to read it.


00:23:46.658 --> 00:23:49.456
- What's that?
- That's the Zodiac at the lake.


00:23:49.561 --> 00:23:50.960
What's the story with the kid?


00:23:51.062 --> 00:23:53.462
He seems a little touched
or medicated or...


00:23:53.565 --> 00:23:54.691
- Graysmith?
- Yeah, what is it?


00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.290
He's a fucking boy scout.


00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:58.596
He doesn't smoke,
he doesn't drink, he doesn't curse.


00:23:58.703 --> 00:24:00.136
- And he's back.
- I knew it.


00:24:00.238 --> 00:24:01.569
"Man is the most
dangerous animal of all. "


00:24:01.673 --> 00:24:02.765
I knew that
I heard that from somewhere.


00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:05.172
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


00:24:05.277 --> 00:24:08.246
It's a movie about a Count
who hunts people for sport.


00:24:08.346 --> 00:24:09.370
People.


00:24:09.481 --> 00:24:11.449
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


00:24:12.217 --> 00:24:14.651
- Who's that?
- That's Count Zaroff.


00:24:14.753 --> 00:24:16.846
Zaroff? With a "Z"?


00:24:19.524 --> 00:24:21.253
<i>And that will be
all for the news on the 20.</i>


00:24:21.359 --> 00:24:23.657
<i>We've got curfews in effect tonight
for the following counties:</i>


00:24:23.762 --> 00:24:27.892
<i>Napa, Solano, Contra Costa,
Alameda, Marin, and San Mateo.</i>


00:24:27.999 --> 00:24:30.126
<i>So please, everyone, stay safe.</i>


00:24:30.235 --> 00:24:33.534
<i>Vic in San Francisco, you're on the line.
You're not scared of the Zodiac?</i>


00:24:33.638 --> 00:24:36.698
<i>Heck no,
he's only shooting those farm kids.</i>


00:24:36.808 --> 00:24:39.402
<i>What scares me
is those hippies out in the Haight</i>


00:24:39.511 --> 00:24:41.376
<i>with their free love and weird clothes.</i>


00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:43.471
<i>We've got Alfred from Vacaville.</i>


00:24:43.582 --> 00:24:45.846
<i>You know, I think
that was really offensive.</i>


00:24:45.951 --> 00:24:47.578
<i>It's not just farm kids.</i>


00:24:47.686 --> 00:24:49.551
<i>These are nice, clean-cut young people.</i>


00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:52.088
<i>Hey, nobody's downplaying
the loss of human life here, Alfred.</i>


00:24:52.190 --> 00:24:54.181
<i>Well, that last guy was.</i>


00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:57.125
<i>We have good solid communities
out here in the North Bay.</i>


00:24:57.229 --> 00:25:00.756
<i>Unlike in the city where you have
Satanists running around.</i>


00:25:00.866 --> 00:25:04.324
<i>Well, you bring up a good question.
Is the Zodiac a Satanist?</i>


00:25:04.436 --> 00:25:06.131
<i>Amber from Oakland,
what do you think?</i>


00:25:06.238 --> 00:25:07.432
<i>I don't really know,</i>


00:25:07.539 --> 00:25:10.633
<i>but I thought that code
they printed didn't look very Christian.</i>


00:25:10.742 --> 00:25:13.438
<i>But I think the bigger problem
is that the papers shouldn't have printed</i>


00:25:13.545 --> 00:25:15.376
<i>anything that the Zodiac
has been doing.</i>


00:25:15.480 --> 00:25:18.608
<i>That they're just printing
all that stuff to sell more newspapers.</i>


00:25:18.717 --> 00:25:20.878
<i>Well, the Zodiac did demand
they print his letters</i>


00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:22.578
<i>or he'd kill more people.</i>


00:25:22.687 --> 00:25:23.984
<i>Yeah, but he would have
done it anyway,</i>


00:25:24.089 --> 00:25:25.647
<i>whether they printed it or not, I think.</i>


00:25:25.757 --> 00:25:27.190
<i>An interesting point.</i>


00:25:27.292 --> 00:25:29.226
<i>So, what do you think he'll do next?</i>


00:25:49.981 --> 00:25:53.542
<i>- San Francisco Police Department.
- Yes. There's a fight in a cab!</i>


00:25:53.652 --> 00:25:54.880
<i>What is your location?</i>


00:25:54.986 --> 00:25:57.955
<i>3398 Washington,
at the corner of Cherry.</i>


00:25:58.056 --> 00:25:59.785
<i>One's drunk and
we think he's robbing him.</i>


00:25:59.891 --> 00:26:03.019
<i>- Is the crime still in progress?
- Yes, please hurry.</i>


00:26:04.729 --> 00:26:06.162
Oh, my God, look!


00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:30.448
Nuts!


00:26:33.758 --> 00:26:35.555
Whoever this is,
you owe me a new lamp.


00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:38.288
<i>Cabbie's been shot
three blocks from the Presidio.</i>


00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:40.591
Well, it wasn't me.
I've been with my bride all night.


00:26:40.699 --> 00:26:43.668
- She can vouch.
- Go put on the Folgers.


00:26:43.768 --> 00:26:45.167
<i>You'll pick me up?</i>


00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.101
Let me just describe
the lamp you're gonna buy me.


00:26:55.947 --> 00:26:58.882
- I just got to sleep.
- Suspect's Negro, male adult.


00:26:58.984 --> 00:27:01.475
Walt's on scene, locked up the cab
and secured the crowd.


00:27:01.586 --> 00:27:04.487
Seriously, dead asleep.
I lost feeling in my arm and everything.


00:27:04.589 --> 00:27:05.886
Crackers.


00:27:09.761 --> 00:27:11.752
You ever try Japanese food?


00:27:11.863 --> 00:27:14.525
What do you mean, like teriyaki?
No, like the urchin.


00:27:14.633 --> 00:27:16.999
- Raw fish.
- I'm eating here, Bill.


00:27:18.370 --> 00:27:21.339
- I always wanted to try it.
- So, why don't you?


00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:23.407
Haven't got around to it.


00:27:39.024 --> 00:27:42.152
Evening, gents.
A lovely night for a botched robbery.


00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:44.820
Yeah, third this week.
Must be end of summer rush.


00:27:44.929 --> 00:27:48.057
I got foot patrols going through the park,
dogs are on the way.


00:27:48.166 --> 00:27:52.466
The victim's name is Paul Stine.
Dousette pronounced him at 10:10.


00:27:52.570 --> 00:27:54.663
Suspect fired one shot
to the back of the head.


00:27:54.773 --> 00:27:56.673
Driver's wallet
and car keys are missing.


00:27:56.775 --> 00:27:57.799
How'd you know his name?


00:27:57.909 --> 00:28:00.844
Leroy, there, came down
from Yellow Cab to ID him.


00:28:00.945 --> 00:28:02.503
Neighborhood's pretty high-end
for this kind of thing,


00:28:02.614 --> 00:28:04.815
so I already set up transpo for the cab.


00:28:04.916 --> 00:28:06.383
- Coroner's here.
- Any witnesses?


00:28:06.484 --> 00:28:09.920
Kids who called it in
saw the suspect from that window.


00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:11.511
- Did they hear a shot?
- No.


00:28:11.623 --> 00:28:12.920
They first saw him in the front seat,


00:28:13.024 --> 00:28:14.719
thought he was a drunk
fighting with the driver.


00:28:14.826 --> 00:28:17.795
Oldest kid ran downstairs to get
a better look from the dining room,


00:28:17.896 --> 00:28:19.693
described him as a white male, glasses,


00:28:19.798 --> 00:28:21.993
crew-cut, stocky,
and wearing a dark jacket.


00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:23.897
Wait, I thought someone said
he was black.


00:28:24.002 --> 00:28:25.902
That's the description
that went out to radio cars.


00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:28.939
- We already corrected it.
- Oh, well, that's good.


00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:31.406
- You guys need anything else?
- No. Get out of here.


00:28:31.509 --> 00:28:33.443
Thanks. Happy Birthday.


00:28:33.545 --> 00:28:36.241
- Wait, it's your birthday?
- Yep.


00:28:36.347 --> 00:28:38.474
- That's great. Happy birthday.
- Thanks.


00:28:38.583 --> 00:28:41.575
- Body or scene?
- It's your birthday, I'll take the body.


00:28:41.686 --> 00:28:44.211
Dave, looks like he
wiped the cab down pretty good.


00:28:44.322 --> 00:28:46.313
- We got some blood over here.
- Prints?


00:28:46.424 --> 00:28:48.255
Could very well be.
We'll dust it at the Hall.


00:28:48.359 --> 00:28:51.123
The odd thing is, we also got gloves.


00:28:51.229 --> 00:28:53.629
- Suspect's?
- There's blood on them.


00:28:55.066 --> 00:28:56.260
- Hey, Pete?
- Yeah, Dave.


00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:57.527
You through over there,
can I get in there?


00:28:57.635 --> 00:28:59.262
Yeah, I'm all set.


00:29:00.071 --> 00:29:02.062
- Who rolled him?
- Stewarts.


00:29:09.147 --> 00:29:11.138
I got a single 9mm casing.


00:29:15.653 --> 00:29:17.518
Yeah, Luger.


00:29:17.622 --> 00:29:19.453
Nothing from the crowd.


00:29:19.557 --> 00:29:22.424
Okay.
I'm your shooter, Negro male adult,


00:29:22.527 --> 00:29:25.860
who also happens to be
a stocky, crew-cut Caucasian.


00:29:25.964 --> 00:29:28.489
I flag a cab. I give him this address.


00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.364
Did I give him this address?
Who's got the fare book?


00:29:31.469 --> 00:29:32.800
Right here.


00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:38.007
Washington and Maple.
That's one block east.


00:29:59.030 --> 00:30:00.292
Lighting's the same over here,


00:30:00.398 --> 00:30:02.832
so maybe I see
someone walking their dog.


00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:05.767
You don't want any witnesses
so you tell him to go down a block.


00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:06.928
He pulls over.


00:30:07.038 --> 00:30:08.903
I wait for him to put it in park
because I'm smart


00:30:09.007 --> 00:30:10.372
and I don't want him
hitting the accelerator


00:30:10.475 --> 00:30:11.737
when I shoot him. May I?


00:30:11.843 --> 00:30:14.209
He stops, puts it in park, boom.


00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:17.008
I shoot him on the right side,
he slumps right?


00:30:17.115 --> 00:30:19.106
Maybe you've got your hand
on his collar when you shoot.


00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:20.377
All right. So, either way,


00:30:20.485 --> 00:30:22.180
I just dumped a quart of blood
in the front seat.


00:30:22.287 --> 00:30:25.415
- So, why do you get in the front seat?
- For the money.


00:30:25.523 --> 00:30:26.547
But he's dead.


00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:28.353
You could just reach over the seat,
pull out his wallet.


00:30:28.459 --> 00:30:30.620
You don't have to go
anywhere near the blood.


00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:33.196
So, why'd he get in the front seat?


00:30:33.731 --> 00:30:35.392
- I'm an idiot.
- But you're not an idiot.


00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:37.161
You waited for him to put it in park.


00:30:37.268 --> 00:30:39.463
- Right. Thank you.
- Yeah, sure.


00:30:41.206 --> 00:30:43.037
- Can I see that?
- Yeah.


00:30:43.575 --> 00:30:46.840
I am an idiot.
I just killed a man for $8.25.


00:30:46.945 --> 00:30:51.245
It's his third fare of the night.
Does anyone have any animal crackers?


00:30:51.783 --> 00:30:53.978
- Animal crackers?
- They're in the car.


00:30:54.085 --> 00:30:56.280
I'm saving those for later.


00:30:56.387 --> 00:30:57.547
Fine.


00:31:02.026 --> 00:31:05.723
- Are you a reporter?
- No, I'm Inspector Dave Toschi, SFPD.


00:31:05.830 --> 00:31:08.355
Sir, I was wondering
if I'd be able to talk to your children,


00:31:08.466 --> 00:31:10.696
one at a time and preferably alone?


00:31:10.802 --> 00:31:12.667
They just saw a man murdered.


00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:14.704
I understand.


00:31:14.806 --> 00:31:16.296
It looked like
they were drunk and fighting.


00:31:16.407 --> 00:31:17.704
Yeah, and he had a rag.


00:31:17.809 --> 00:31:20.175
He came around the side of the car
and he was wiping stuff.


00:31:20.278 --> 00:31:23.611
- Did you get a chance to see his face?
- I did.


00:31:23.715 --> 00:31:25.205
Well, sort of.


00:31:26.484 --> 00:31:28.975
Did you remember what he looked like?


00:31:30.488 --> 00:31:32.479
- Normal.
- Yeah.


00:31:32.590 --> 00:31:33.784
"Normal"?


00:31:56.614 --> 00:31:58.172
<i>"This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


00:31:58.283 --> 00:32:00.183
<i>"I am the murderer of the taxi driver</i>


00:32:00.285 --> 00:32:04.187
"over by Washington Street
and Maple Street last night.


00:32:04.289 --> 00:32:06.723
"To prove this, here is
a blood-stained piece of his shirt.


00:32:06.824 --> 00:32:11.761
"I am the same man who did in
the people in the North Bay Area.


00:32:11.863 --> 00:32:14.423
"The S.F. Police could have
caught me last night


00:32:14.532 --> 00:32:16.056
"if they had searched the park properly


00:32:16.167 --> 00:32:19.432
"instead of holding road races
with their motorcicles. "


00:32:19.537 --> 00:32:21.027
- Gentlemen.
- Dave.


00:32:21.139 --> 00:32:23.073
Paul. Where's the shirt?


00:32:24.509 --> 00:32:26.101
Right there, boss.


00:32:27.312 --> 00:32:28.870
There's your rag the kids talked about.


00:32:28.980 --> 00:32:30.971
So he got in the front seat
to tear off a piece of the shirt.


00:32:31.082 --> 00:32:33.482
- Is this on the record?
- Well, what do you think?


00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:35.609
He confirms
the Vallejo and Napa killings.


00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.278
Gets worse.


00:32:37.388 --> 00:32:39.413
Robert, do you have a deadline?


00:32:39.524 --> 00:32:41.651
What does he mean, it gets worse?


00:32:41.759 --> 00:32:43.158
Read the last part.


00:32:43.261 --> 00:32:45.491
"School children make nice targets.


00:32:45.596 --> 00:32:47.894
"I think I shall wipe out
a school bus some morning.


00:32:47.999 --> 00:32:49.660
"Just shoot out the front tire


00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:52.167
"and then pick off the kiddies
as they come bouncing out. "


00:32:52.270 --> 00:32:54.795
Jesus Christ, who's got school buses?
Department of Transportation?


00:32:54.906 --> 00:32:56.806
- School board.
- All right.


00:32:56.908 --> 00:32:59.172
I'm gonna need elimination prints
from your staff.


00:32:59.277 --> 00:33:01.768
Anyone here didn't touch this letter?


00:33:05.783 --> 00:33:08.411
On my way back to my desk.
They have phones, if you want.


00:33:08.519 --> 00:33:10.111
We need to get matches
on blood and fabric.


00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:11.381
I'll call Napa and Vallejo,


00:33:11.489 --> 00:33:13.286
get the letters up to Sherwood
in Sacramento.


00:33:13.391 --> 00:33:16.792
Dave, just one thing.
Is it true they got a print off the cab?


00:33:16.894 --> 00:33:19.226
Yeah, we got a partial in blood.


00:33:20.098 --> 00:33:23.226
- But that is not for publication.
- Hey, hey, come on.


00:33:23.334 --> 00:33:25.564
Hey, it's me.


00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:27.763
Did he say they got a print?


00:33:28.873 --> 00:33:30.067
Partial.


00:33:31.075 --> 00:33:32.133
Whoa.


00:33:33.511 --> 00:33:35.001
Dude, he wears his gun like Bullitt.


00:33:35.113 --> 00:33:37.479
No, McQueen got that from Toschi.


00:33:37.582 --> 00:33:39.311
Does he think that Zodiac's
gonna send another code?


00:33:39.417 --> 00:33:41.248
'Cause I think Zodiac's
gonna send another code.


00:33:41.352 --> 00:33:43.377
Jesus Harold Christ
on rubber crutches, Bobby.


00:33:43.488 --> 00:33:44.512
What are you doing?


00:33:44.622 --> 00:33:45.919
You're doing that thing,
the thing we discussed,


00:33:46.024 --> 00:33:48.515
the thing that I don't like.
Starts with an "L."


00:33:48.626 --> 00:33:50.526
- Oh, looming.
- Yeah.


00:33:50.628 --> 00:33:53.529
In cooperation with SFPD,
we will run the Zodiac letter


00:33:53.631 --> 00:33:56.293
without including the threat
on school children.


00:33:56.401 --> 00:33:58.062
We don't want to start a city-wide panic


00:33:58.169 --> 00:34:01.661
so I'm asking all of you
to please keep this confidential.


00:34:01.773 --> 00:34:03.968
Just go about your daily business.


00:34:04.075 --> 00:34:05.406
Thank you.


00:34:21.125 --> 00:34:24.117
I packed you your carrots
and your soda and peanut butter, okay?


00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:27.163
- Dad, you don't have to wait with me.
- I know.


00:34:34.572 --> 00:34:38.372
You know what? You know what?
I'm gonna drive him today, okay?


00:34:38.876 --> 00:34:40.070
Come on.


00:34:58.262 --> 00:34:59.786
What's that?


00:34:59.897 --> 00:35:02.422
Similarities in the lowercase "r's. "


00:35:11.609 --> 00:35:12.735
And that?


00:35:12.844 --> 00:35:14.812
It is you waiting in the hall
if you speak again.


00:35:14.912 --> 00:35:16.743
I have to concentrate.


00:35:17.148 --> 00:35:18.240
Sorry.


00:35:18.349 --> 00:35:20.317
"Sorry" counts as speaking.


00:35:31.229 --> 00:35:34.198
There are similarities
in the lowercase "r's. "


00:35:38.269 --> 00:35:40.703
We have to release the bus threat.


00:35:41.305 --> 00:35:43.933
- It'll screw us.
- We're already screwed.


00:35:44.041 --> 00:35:46.271
We just went from
"Routine Cabbie Shooting"


00:35:46.377 --> 00:35:48.538
to "Mass Murderer Targets Kids. "


00:35:56.254 --> 00:35:59.417
<i>The Zodiac Killer
has come to San Francisco.</i>


00:35:59.524 --> 00:36:02.550
<i>Confirmation tonight, from the
San Francisco Police Department</i>


00:36:02.660 --> 00:36:04.594
<i>that in his latest haunting letter,</i>


00:36:04.695 --> 00:36:07.892
<i>which takes credit for the murder
of cab driver Paul Stine,</i>


00:36:07.999 --> 00:36:11.366
<i>the Zodiac has threatened to,
"Wipe out a school bus</i>


00:36:11.469 --> 00:36:14.802
<i>"and pick off the kiddies
as they come bouncing out. "</i>


00:36:18.276 --> 00:36:20.938
<i>If you think you might know
who the Zodiac is,</i>


00:36:21.045 --> 00:36:24.708
<i>you can call the San Francisco
Police Department's newest tip line.</i>


00:36:48.339 --> 00:36:51.274
Press conference is at 4:00.
We got to give them something.


00:36:51.375 --> 00:36:52.967
We're coordinating
with the school board,


00:36:53.077 --> 00:36:55.068
and we expect
a break in the case very soon.


00:36:55.179 --> 00:36:56.942
- What do we really got?
- We're swamped.


00:36:57.048 --> 00:36:58.413
When they can't get anyone
on the tip line


00:36:58.516 --> 00:37:00.211
they call the switchboard
and keep getting put through.


00:37:00.318 --> 00:37:01.307
You got any hard suspects?


00:37:01.419 --> 00:37:04.115
About 90 an hour. I'm up to around 500.


00:37:04.222 --> 00:37:05.348
Well, can't you narrow it down?


00:37:05.456 --> 00:37:07.617
I would love to,
if I could get out of this...


00:37:07.725 --> 00:37:11.217
- Homicide, please hold.
- Yeah, hold, please.


00:37:11.329 --> 00:37:13.194
We're gonna need to tell them
we got the entire force on this.


00:37:13.297 --> 00:37:14.423
How many men can you give me?


00:37:14.532 --> 00:37:16.523
Well, right now, it's you and Bill
and Monday's a school day.


00:37:16.634 --> 00:37:18.534
Yeah, I know, Chief.
I have three daughters of my own.


00:37:18.636 --> 00:37:20.570
Yeah, I know. Where's Armstrong?


00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.138
He's on the phone with Vallejo.


00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:24.174
We're playing catch up, Jack.


00:37:24.275 --> 00:37:26.766
I'd like to set up a meeting
with your survivor, Michael Mageau.


00:37:26.877 --> 00:37:28.469
I can't. He skipped town.


00:37:28.579 --> 00:37:31.207
The only guy who's seen Zodiac
without a mask is missing?


00:37:31.315 --> 00:37:34.443
When he was still in the hospital
we could show him lineups all day long.


00:37:34.552 --> 00:37:35.951
As soon as he got out, he split.


00:37:36.053 --> 00:37:37.077
<i>Really? Why?</i>


00:37:37.188 --> 00:37:39.486
I don't think he wanted
to have anything to do with this.


00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:41.558
<i>Can you send us everything
that you have?</i>


00:37:41.659 --> 00:37:44.492
Well, the road goes both ways.


00:37:44.595 --> 00:37:47.723
Now, we need that print
you lifted from the cab


00:37:47.832 --> 00:37:49.766
<i>and we should have been in
on the handwriting.</i>


00:37:49.867 --> 00:37:52.131
I apologize.
Things have been moving fast.


00:37:52.236 --> 00:37:54.966
<i>Who should I talk to in Napa
so we can coordinate?</i>


00:37:55.072 --> 00:37:56.198
Talk to Ken Narlow.


00:37:56.307 --> 00:37:58.172
We really should have been in
on the handwriting.


00:37:58.276 --> 00:38:00.744
<i>I apologize.
Things have been moving fast.</i>


00:38:00.845 --> 00:38:02.278
<i>Listen, we're gonna need
your scene photos.</i>


00:38:02.380 --> 00:38:03.404
Can't help you.


00:38:03.514 --> 00:38:05.448
<i>Ken, I don't want to get into
a jurisdictional thing here.</i>


00:38:05.549 --> 00:38:08.143
No, no, no, no, no.
We didn't have a crime scene.


00:38:08.252 --> 00:38:11.483
The ranger that found the kids literally
swept everything into a picnic blanket.


00:38:11.589 --> 00:38:13.284
<i>All we have are the Wing Walker prints.</i>


00:38:13.391 --> 00:38:14.483
The what?


00:38:14.592 --> 00:38:16.287
Boot prints to and from the crime scene


00:38:16.394 --> 00:38:18.692
were made by size
10-and-a-half Wing Walkers,


00:38:18.796 --> 00:38:21.731
military-style boots
sold only at military PXs


00:38:22.066 --> 00:38:24.091
designed to walk
on the wings of planes.


00:38:24.201 --> 00:38:26.692
<i>And you can't buy at a PX
without a military ID,</i>


00:38:26.804 --> 00:38:28.738
so our suspect could be military.


00:38:28.839 --> 00:38:30.602
Did you guys narrow your list off of this?


00:38:30.708 --> 00:38:32.801
<i>- Yeah.
- Did Vallejo?</i>


00:38:32.910 --> 00:38:35.003
I don't know. I don't work in Vallejo.
I work here.


00:38:35.112 --> 00:38:37.239
Great. I'm gonna need photos
of those boot prints.


00:38:37.348 --> 00:38:39.316
<i>Sure, if you send me the handwriting.</i>


00:38:39.417 --> 00:38:41.009
I thought Questioned Documents
already did.


00:38:41.118 --> 00:38:42.608
Nope. Vallejo's got them, not us.


00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:44.711
All right.
I'll have Questioned Documents...


00:38:44.822 --> 00:38:46.722
Forget it. I'll telefax it to you.


00:38:46.824 --> 00:38:48.291
We don't have telefax yet.


00:38:48.392 --> 00:38:50.986
<i>- Okay, I'll put it in the mail.
- We'll mail ours, too.</i>


00:38:51.095 --> 00:38:52.756
And call Mulanax in Vallejo.


00:38:52.863 --> 00:38:54.956
- Maybe he can get you a mimeo.
- Right.


00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:57.432
Why don't you just get a photo
off the original plaster cast?


00:38:57.535 --> 00:38:59.628
We'd have to wait,
because they don't have a fax.


00:38:59.737 --> 00:39:01.170
<i>We don't have a fax, either.</i>


00:39:01.272 --> 00:39:03.001
Look, I'm just trying
to get us coordinated.


00:39:03.107 --> 00:39:04.574
Have you called Solano Sheriff's Office?


00:39:04.675 --> 00:39:06.302
Why would I call Solano?


00:39:06.410 --> 00:39:10.005
<i>Because the two kids that got killed
last Christmas were Solano's.</i>


00:39:10.114 --> 00:39:11.308
I thought they were Vallejo.


00:39:11.415 --> 00:39:12.712
No, they were over the county line


00:39:12.817 --> 00:39:15.012
so you're gonna need
to coordinate with them, too.


00:39:15.119 --> 00:39:16.552
Okay.


00:39:16.654 --> 00:39:17.746
Bill.


00:39:18.456 --> 00:39:20.321
Can I have a word with you?


00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:25.353
Where did you see this guy?


00:39:26.163 --> 00:39:28.597
We got the call to circle the scene
and look for a Negro male adult.


00:39:28.699 --> 00:39:30.166
Where was he?


00:39:30.267 --> 00:39:32.701
On Jackson. Heading east.
About the middle of the block.


00:39:32.803 --> 00:39:34.828
And this is three minutes
after the shooting?


00:39:34.939 --> 00:39:36.099
Give or take. Yeah.


00:39:36.207 --> 00:39:38.437
- And you were heading east or west?
- We were going west.


00:39:38.542 --> 00:39:40.772
All right, so you're
on Jackson going west.


00:39:40.878 --> 00:39:44.006
So the cab was one block
catty-corner southwest?


00:39:44.115 --> 00:39:45.776
- Correct.
- Did you slow down?


00:39:45.883 --> 00:39:47.544
- Of course we slowed down.
- All right.


00:39:47.651 --> 00:39:49.949
Listen, Dispatch said
it was a Negro male.


00:39:50.054 --> 00:39:51.316
That was corrected.


00:39:51.422 --> 00:39:54.084
No, but at the time
they hadn't changed it.


00:39:54.191 --> 00:39:56.250
This guy was white.


00:39:56.360 --> 00:39:58.191
Right, not in a hurry.
Kind of lumbering along like...


00:39:58.295 --> 00:40:00.889
Lumbering?
What do you mean, "lumbering"?


00:40:02.199 --> 00:40:04.895
- Shuffling.
- Stocky? Had a crew cut?


00:40:05.870 --> 00:40:08.100
Yeah, that's all correct.


00:40:08.205 --> 00:40:09.934
Listen, it was dark.


00:40:10.875 --> 00:40:12.900
The guy was wearing a dark jacket.
There's no way...


00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:15.501
He would have been covered in blood.


00:40:17.114 --> 00:40:18.706
Did you stop him?


00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:22.548
Did you talk to him?


00:40:23.154 --> 00:40:25.088
- Yes? No?
- No.


00:40:25.990 --> 00:40:27.480
You need to get with a sketch artist.


00:40:27.591 --> 00:40:30.583
We have to put out
a new composite right away.


00:40:33.497 --> 00:40:36.557
<i>Five persons have been murdered
in the San Francisco area,</i>


00:40:36.734 --> 00:40:38.133
<i>and in each case the killer...</i>


00:40:38.235 --> 00:40:40.726
<i>"I shall wipe out a school bus
some morning... "</i>


00:40:40.838 --> 00:40:42.465
<i>San Francisco police...</i>


00:40:44.341 --> 00:40:47.071
<i>...to see the Stones in concert
this Sunday.</i>


00:40:47.178 --> 00:40:49.237
<i>The new letters
from the Zodiac Killer were sent to</i>


00:40:49.346 --> 00:40:51.280
<i>the City room of the
San Francisco Chronicle.</i>


00:40:52.750 --> 00:40:55.275
Looming. No looming.


00:40:55.386 --> 00:40:58.480
- Have you considered the water theory?
- What?


00:40:58.589 --> 00:41:01.251
Geographically, every attack
takes place near a body of water


00:41:01.358 --> 00:41:02.655
- or a water-based name.
- This is your water theory?


00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:05.194
Lake Berryessa. Blue Rock Springs.
Lake Herman.


00:41:05.296 --> 00:41:07.457
Wash-ington and Cherry?


00:41:09.433 --> 00:41:11.025
You think?


00:41:11.135 --> 00:41:12.159
No.


00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:13.668
I'm reading this book,


00:41:13.771 --> 00:41:15.398
<i>Homicide Investigation
by Lemoyne Snyder...</i>


00:41:15.506 --> 00:41:16.905
- "Leymone. "
- ... and he says you look for patterns,


00:41:17.007 --> 00:41:19.100
- so I'm looking for patterns.
- No.


00:41:19.210 --> 00:41:21.542
You can't think of this case
in normal police terms.


00:41:21.645 --> 00:41:23.806
- Why not?
- You got four crime scenes:


00:41:23.914 --> 00:41:26.815
Solano, Vallejo, Berryessa, and here.


00:41:26.917 --> 00:41:30.944
Not a single usable print
at the first three or in any of the letters?


00:41:31.055 --> 00:41:34.547
How does our master criminal come
to the city and leave a bloody latent?


00:41:34.658 --> 00:41:37.218
I mean, assuming the gloves are his,


00:41:37.328 --> 00:41:39.023
he shoots the cabbie
and then takes them off?


00:41:39.129 --> 00:41:40.289
<i>So it's not his print?</i>


00:41:40.397 --> 00:41:42.160
Maybe, maybe not.
You're missing the point.


00:41:42.266 --> 00:41:44.860
- The point is the first attack...
- David Faraday and Betty Jensen.


00:41:44.969 --> 00:41:46.527
They both die.


00:41:46.637 --> 00:41:49.105
From there on out,
he only manages to kill the girls.


00:41:49.206 --> 00:41:51.140
- Not for lack of trying.
- Not for lack of trying.


00:41:51.242 --> 00:41:54.769
Mageau lives, Ferrin dies.
Hartnell lives, Shepard dies.


00:41:54.879 --> 00:41:58.246
He gets so caught up with the women
he forgets to finish off the men.


00:41:58.349 --> 00:42:00.681
Plus, they're all couples
and all on lover's lanes.


00:42:00.784 --> 00:42:02.615
- Paul Stine is not.
- Exactly.


00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:04.847
Single, male cab driver
on Washington and Cherry doesn't fit.


00:42:04.955 --> 00:42:06.320
Doesn't fit.


00:42:07.291 --> 00:42:09.555
So, why does Zodiac kill him?


00:42:12.396 --> 00:42:14.387
He's breaking the pattern.


00:42:23.607 --> 00:42:24.631
Yeah?


00:42:24.742 --> 00:42:27.973
<i>Someone claiming to be Zodiac
called Oakland PD a half-hour ago.</i>


00:42:28.078 --> 00:42:31.673
<i>He says he's gonna call in on Jim
Dunbar's morning show in three hours.</i>


00:42:31.916 --> 00:42:32.974
On television?


00:42:33.083 --> 00:42:35.142
<i>He wants Melvin Belli on
to counsel him.</i>


00:42:35.252 --> 00:42:37.345
All right. All right.
Let's go wake up Melvin.


00:42:39.823 --> 00:42:41.688
Animal crackers?


00:42:41.792 --> 00:42:43.089
Glove box.


00:42:43.193 --> 00:42:44.888
Are these windows bulletproof?


00:42:44.995 --> 00:42:47.520
Yes, Melvin.
You don't have to lie down back there.


00:42:47.631 --> 00:42:48.825
This man is a marksman,


00:42:48.933 --> 00:42:51.766
could snuff me out
at a moment's notice.


00:42:51.869 --> 00:42:53.234
Are you sure you're up for this?


00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:57.774
Don't you worry about me, Inspector.
I'll be fine when the lights are on.


00:42:57.875 --> 00:42:59.604
This man has asked for my help.


00:42:59.710 --> 00:43:01.769
The man you're worrying about
snuffing you out?


00:43:01.879 --> 00:43:03.813
What are these, cookies?


00:43:05.549 --> 00:43:07.574
Dear Lord, do you ever clean this car?


00:43:07.685 --> 00:43:11.018
- Shit.
- KGO must have tipped other stations.


00:43:20.965 --> 00:43:23.763
<i>Get him talking.
Convince him to meet you somewhere.</i>


00:43:23.867 --> 00:43:25.391
If you see an opportunity,


00:43:25.502 --> 00:43:28.130
we want you to suggest
Old St. Mary's Church in Chinatown.


00:43:28.238 --> 00:43:29.398
You'll be tracing the call?


00:43:29.506 --> 00:43:32.600
Pacific Telephone says you need to
keep him on the line for 15 minutes.


00:43:32.710 --> 00:43:34.940
We can do that, can't we, Jim?


00:43:37.314 --> 00:43:39.646
Fifteen seconds. Clear the set.


00:43:46.023 --> 00:43:48.218
Here you go, you drunken reprobate.


00:43:48.325 --> 00:43:52.125
<i>We interrupt our regular program
to bring you this news bulletin.</i>


00:43:52.229 --> 00:43:54.197
<i>Welcome to this special edition
of our show</i>


00:43:54.298 --> 00:43:56.163
<i>in which we are joined
by attorney Melvin Belli</i>


00:43:56.266 --> 00:43:59.633
<i>who the Zodiac Killer
personally requested to appear.</i>


00:43:59.737 --> 00:44:01.568
Finish up, buddy, and put it in the sink.


00:44:01.672 --> 00:44:04.470
<i>- Good morning, Melvin.
- Good morning, Jim.</i>


00:44:04.642 --> 00:44:08.009
<i>So, the phone lines are open.
Mr. Belli is here.</i>


00:44:08.112 --> 00:44:09.136
<i>Here to help, Jim.</i>


00:44:09.246 --> 00:44:11.077
<i>Yes. Here to help.</i>


00:44:11.181 --> 00:44:15.880
<i>And we ask the public not to call in,
so that the Zodiac himself can reach us.</i>


00:44:24.962 --> 00:44:28.363
<i>I saw your Star Trek, by the way.
It was excellent.</i>


00:44:28.465 --> 00:44:30.399
A shame about the show.


00:44:30.501 --> 00:44:31.968
Good people.


00:44:32.069 --> 00:44:35.698
You know, I've often thought of
becoming an actor full-time.


00:44:35.806 --> 00:44:37.171
What was your character's name?


00:44:37.274 --> 00:44:39.469
<i>- Gorgon.
- Gorgon. That's right.</i>


00:44:41.011 --> 00:44:42.911
Roll the tape. Get the tape.


00:44:43.013 --> 00:44:45.277
Jim, we have a call. We're going live.


00:44:46.784 --> 00:44:47.978
Hello?


00:44:51.555 --> 00:44:53.716
Hello? This is Melvin Belli.


00:44:54.892 --> 00:44:56.757
Who am I speaking with?


00:44:57.161 --> 00:44:59.561
<i>This is the Zodiac speaking.</i>


00:45:02.633 --> 00:45:06.501
Is there something I can call you
that's a little less ominous?


00:45:08.539 --> 00:45:09.836
<i>Sam.</i>


00:45:10.207 --> 00:45:12.175
<i>- Sam.
- Yes.</i>


00:45:12.276 --> 00:45:15.734
Sam, do you think
you need medical care?


00:45:15.846 --> 00:45:17.711
<i>Medical, not mental.</i>


00:45:17.815 --> 00:45:20.113
Do you have health problems?


00:45:20.217 --> 00:45:21.946
<i>I'm sick. I have headaches.</i>


00:45:22.052 --> 00:45:23.781
Headaches?


00:45:23.887 --> 00:45:25.218
I have headaches, too,


00:45:25.322 --> 00:45:28.018
but a chiropractor stopped them
a week ago.


00:45:28.125 --> 00:45:29.922
I think I can help you, Sam.


00:45:32.362 --> 00:45:33.624
Sam?


00:45:35.566 --> 00:45:38.034
He knows they're tracing his calls.


00:45:41.705 --> 00:45:45.732
<i>Sam, we'd like you to know
that we are not tracing these calls.</i>


00:45:45.843 --> 00:45:50.075
<i>It's a long, difficult process
and ineffective with these short calls.</i>


00:45:55.586 --> 00:45:56.644
Sam?


00:45:58.922 --> 00:46:02.016
We're not tracing these calls.
You have my word.


00:46:02.926 --> 00:46:04.086
<i>Okay.</i>


00:46:04.595 --> 00:46:07.860
<i>Sam, you need to tell me
what your problem is.</i>


00:46:07.965 --> 00:46:09.830
<i>I don't want to go to the gas chamber.</i>


00:46:09.933 --> 00:46:12.424
<i>I have headaches.
I kill, I don't get them.</i>


00:46:12.536 --> 00:46:13.867
That is fucked up!


00:46:13.971 --> 00:46:17.429
<i>You want to live, don't you?
Well, this is your passport.</i>


00:46:17.541 --> 00:46:19.338
<i>How long have you been
having these headaches?</i>


00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:21.240
<i>Since I killed a kid.</i>


00:46:22.646 --> 00:46:24.011
<i>I don't want to be hurt.</i>


00:46:24.114 --> 00:46:26.344
- Why is he calling?
- Hey, just a second, buddy.


00:46:26.450 --> 00:46:28.111
<i>You won't get hurt if you talk to me.</i>


00:46:28.218 --> 00:46:31.210
And you're not going
to the gas chamber.


00:46:31.321 --> 00:46:33.983
I wouldn't think they would ask
for capital punishment.


00:46:34.091 --> 00:46:35.956
<i>We should ask the District Attorney.</i>


00:46:36.059 --> 00:46:38.118
<i>Do you want me to do that, Sam?</i>


00:46:38.228 --> 00:46:40.924
<i>Do you want me to talk
to the District Attorney?</i>


00:46:44.802 --> 00:46:46.531
What was that, Sam?


00:46:47.538 --> 00:46:49.631
<i>I did not say anything.</i>


00:46:49.740 --> 00:46:51.640
<i>We heard a scream.</i>


00:46:52.442 --> 00:46:54.569
<i>That was my headache.</i>


00:46:55.379 --> 00:46:58.348
You sound like you're in
a great deal of pain.


00:46:59.116 --> 00:47:02.142
<i>My head aches. I'm so sick.</i>


00:47:04.021 --> 00:47:05.511
<i>I'm gonna kill them.</i>


00:47:05.622 --> 00:47:08.455
<i>- Oh, okay.
- I'm gonna kill those kids!</i>


00:47:08.559 --> 00:47:10.151
Fantastic.


00:47:12.729 --> 00:47:14.128
<i>Sam?</i>


00:47:15.666 --> 00:47:19.898
<i>- Let's meet and talk. Just us.
- Okay.</i>


00:47:20.037 --> 00:47:22.699
How about Old St. Mary's Church
in Chinatown?


00:47:22.806 --> 00:47:24.103
<i>No.</i>


00:47:24.208 --> 00:47:28.076
<i>In front of the Daly City
St. Vincent de Paul at 10:30.</i>


00:47:28.178 --> 00:47:29.907
I'll see you there.


00:47:31.682 --> 00:47:33.616
Take care of yourself, Sam.


00:47:57.808 --> 00:47:59.139
My, my, my.


00:47:59.243 --> 00:48:02.440
You fellows certainly know
how to put on a secret meeting.


00:48:06.917 --> 00:48:09.750
<i>I don't want to go to the gas chamber.
I have headaches.</i>


00:48:09.853 --> 00:48:11.878
<i>I kill, I don't get them.</i>


00:48:11.989 --> 00:48:13.616
No, it's not him.


00:48:14.691 --> 00:48:17.819
It's the voice.
The voice is too high. It's too young.


00:48:17.928 --> 00:48:20.624
All right.
Thanks for coming down, Bryan.


00:48:21.632 --> 00:48:23.463
That's okay. I got it.


00:48:29.673 --> 00:48:30.901
They pulled off the trace.


00:48:31.008 --> 00:48:34.068
Our Daly City no-show
called from a mental institution.


00:48:34.177 --> 00:48:36.042
Oakland PD's operator is sure


00:48:36.146 --> 00:48:38.614
the man she talked to
had a deeper voice.


00:48:38.715 --> 00:48:39.875
Calmer.


00:48:40.717 --> 00:48:42.878
Might have actually been him.


00:48:49.126 --> 00:48:52.061
"So I shall change
my way of collecting slaves.


00:48:52.462 --> 00:48:55.898
"I shall no longer announce to anyone
when I commit my murders.


00:48:55.999 --> 00:48:59.196
"They shall look like routine robberies,
killings of anger


00:48:59.303 --> 00:49:02.272
"and a few fake accidents, et cetera.


00:49:02.372 --> 00:49:03.705
"The police shall never catch me


00:49:03.807 --> 00:49:06.139
"because I have been
too clever for them.


00:49:06.243 --> 00:49:09.679
"I look like the description passed out
only when I do my thing.


00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:12.908
"The rest of the time
I look entirely different.


00:49:13.016 --> 00:49:17.817
"I shall not tell you what
my disguise consists of when I kill.


00:49:17.921 --> 00:49:20.446
"As of yet I have left no
fingerprints behind me,


00:49:20.557 --> 00:49:23.048
"contrary to what the police say.


00:49:23.160 --> 00:49:25.526
"I wear transparent fingertips.


00:49:26.496 --> 00:49:31.229
"All it is is two coats of airplane cement
coated on my fingertips.


00:49:31.335 --> 00:49:35.795
"I enjoy needling the blue pigs.
Hey, blue pig, I was in the park.


00:49:35.906 --> 00:49:41.367
"You were using fire trucks to mask
the sound of your cruising prowl cars.


00:49:41.478 --> 00:49:42.911
"Hey, pig, doesn't it rile you up


00:49:43.013 --> 00:49:46.107
"to have your nose
rubbed in your booboos?


00:49:46.216 --> 00:49:49.276
"If you cops think I am going to take
on a bus the way I stated I was,


00:49:49.386 --> 00:49:52.583
"you deserve to have holes
in your heads. "


00:49:54.558 --> 00:49:56.719
And you need to look at this.


00:49:59.596 --> 00:50:01.962
"Take one bag of
ammonium nitrate fertilizer,


00:50:02.065 --> 00:50:03.726
"one gallon of stove oil,


00:50:03.834 --> 00:50:05.961
"and dump a few bags
of gravel on top... "


00:50:06.069 --> 00:50:07.798
- Okay.
- It's a bomb.


00:50:07.904 --> 00:50:09.667
Okay. We gotta call the Army
and see if this


00:50:09.773 --> 00:50:12.503
science experiment could actually work.


00:50:12.609 --> 00:50:14.133
Another cipher.


00:50:16.380 --> 00:50:19.042
- When did these arrive?
- They arrived this morning.


00:50:19.149 --> 00:50:20.548
Are you planning to publish?


00:50:20.650 --> 00:50:21.844
Robert.


00:50:23.353 --> 00:50:25.150
We should have a drink.


00:50:29.192 --> 00:50:30.557
Thank you.


00:50:32.662 --> 00:50:34.892
So, tell me about yourself.


