- Do you know who Paul Avery is?
- Sounds kind of familiar.


01:07:15.398 --> 01:07:17.127
He's the writer
that the Zodiac threatened.


01:07:17.233 --> 01:07:18.700
Oh, yeah, I saw that on TV.


01:07:18.801 --> 01:07:21.668
Well, I work near him
and he's going down tonight


01:07:21.771 --> 01:07:24.934
to track an anonymous tipster
down in Riverside.


01:07:26.108 --> 01:07:28.167
Where is Riverside?


01:07:28.277 --> 01:07:29.744
It's near L.A.


01:07:29.845 --> 01:07:33.440
Oh, wow. I don't think Paul knows
that it's that far away.


01:07:35.651 --> 01:07:37.642
Sounds kind of dangerous.


01:07:38.921 --> 01:07:41.822
Yeah. How do you mean?


01:07:41.924 --> 01:07:44.324
Well, you said it was
an anonymous tip, right?


01:07:44.427 --> 01:07:45.860
Yeah.


01:07:45.961 --> 01:07:49.488
So it could be an ambush.
I mean, it could be the Zodiac.


01:07:51.033 --> 01:07:53.433
Don't you think it's kind of stupid?


01:07:53.536 --> 01:07:56.164
Yeah, yeah. Well, Paul has a gun.


01:08:00.009 --> 01:08:02.477
So, do you know what's good here?


01:08:04.313 --> 01:08:06.440
I've never been here before.


01:08:08.584 --> 01:08:10.552
The pasta, spaghetti?


01:08:12.288 --> 01:08:14.347
Are you ready to order yet?


01:08:15.424 --> 01:08:18.222
Yeah, I'll have the penne vodka.
But could you do it in a cream sauce?


01:08:18.327 --> 01:08:19.624
Of course.


01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:26.795
Maybe give us another minute?


01:08:28.671 --> 01:08:30.605
Do you have any change?


01:08:30.706 --> 01:08:32.867
Oh, wait, no wait, hold on.


01:08:32.975 --> 01:08:34.499
Nope. That's a penny.


01:08:34.610 --> 01:08:36.009
Do you have to make a phone call?


01:08:36.112 --> 01:08:39.570
Yeah, you know,
when you were saying that the Zodiac...


01:08:40.049 --> 01:08:41.846
You know, when you said it
was dangerous, I just thought


01:08:41.951 --> 01:08:43.976
- that it is dangerous, and it's...
- Stupid?


01:08:44.086 --> 01:08:45.383
Stupid. And I just thought


01:08:45.488 --> 01:08:49.481
that I should call his wife
and just see if she's heard from him.


01:08:51.861 --> 01:08:53.294
I have some change.


01:09:12.481 --> 01:09:15.780
Okay. Well, she said
she'd call when she heard from him.


01:09:15.885 --> 01:09:17.318
- Good.
- Yeah.


01:09:18.721 --> 01:09:22.157
Melanie, I should really go home
and wait for the call.


01:09:25.294 --> 01:09:28.752
Is this some sleazy plan
to get me to go home with you?


01:09:29.465 --> 01:09:30.932
What? No.


01:09:33.435 --> 01:09:35.403
I'll get the food to go.


01:09:37.106 --> 01:09:38.232
Hello!


01:09:54.456 --> 01:09:57.289
Hi! I'm supposed
to meet somebody here.


01:10:15.544 --> 01:10:16.943
Anything?


01:10:20.583 --> 01:10:21.845
You don't have to stay.


01:10:21.951 --> 01:10:23.384
Are you kidding?


01:10:23.485 --> 01:10:26.579
This is the most interesting date
I've ever had.


01:10:30.859 --> 01:10:31.951
<i>- Paul?
- Robert?</i>


01:10:32.061 --> 01:10:33.619
- Yes.
- You sitting down?


01:10:33.729 --> 01:10:34.821
<i>Yes.</i>


01:10:34.930 --> 01:10:36.727
You're not gonna believe this.


01:10:36.832 --> 01:10:37.821
Dave!


01:10:37.933 --> 01:10:40.527
<i>In a bizarre twist,
the hunted has become hunter.</i>


01:10:40.636 --> 01:10:44.402
<i>San Francisco Chronicle reporter
and Zodiac target Paul Avery</i>


01:10:44.506 --> 01:10:46.565
<i>claims to have uncovered
new information</i>


01:10:46.675 --> 01:10:51.135
<i>regarding the only unsolved homicide
in Riverside County's history,</i>


01:10:51.247 --> 01:10:54.410
<i>a 1966 Southern California murder,</i>


01:10:54.516 --> 01:10:57.576
<i>that Avery now believes
was the Zodiac's first victim.</i>


01:10:57.686 --> 01:10:58.710
What?


01:10:58.821 --> 01:11:00.049
- He didn't call you about this?
- Hang on!


01:11:00.155 --> 01:11:01.645
<i>The Riverside killer
wrote to the press letters</i>


01:11:01.757 --> 01:11:05.386
<i>that I then took personally to
the Office of Questioned Documents.</i>


01:11:05.494 --> 01:11:07.655
<i>And what did this expert tell you?</i>


01:11:07.763 --> 01:11:09.287
<i>What I knew in my gut, Ron.</i>


01:11:09.398 --> 01:11:11.832
<i>The handwriting matches Zodiac's.</i>


01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:14.266
How'd he get the evidence
out of Riverside?


01:11:14.370 --> 01:11:16.565
He took it to Sherwood
without telling us, the son of a bitch.


01:11:16.672 --> 01:11:17.866
You know how bad this looks?


01:11:17.973 --> 01:11:20.168
Hey, how do we know
that this lead is real?


01:11:20.276 --> 01:11:22.540
It's very real. You know how I know?


01:11:22.645 --> 01:11:24.510
Because I saw it on TV.


01:11:31.620 --> 01:11:32.746
Dave.


01:11:33.155 --> 01:11:34.247
Hi.


01:11:34.356 --> 01:11:36.483
Dave, you know Mel Nicolai.
He's working the case for Justice.


01:11:36.592 --> 01:11:37.752
Good to see you, Mel.


01:11:37.860 --> 01:11:39.725
All due respect,
can someone explain to me


01:11:39.828 --> 01:11:41.455
why I'm reading
about breaks in this case


01:11:41.563 --> 01:11:43.394
<i>in the Chronicle instead
of getting calls from you?</i>


01:11:43.499 --> 01:11:44.557
We got screwed.


01:11:44.667 --> 01:11:45.827
Dave, come on.


01:11:45.934 --> 01:11:47.902
You do get your name in the paper a lot.
People talk.


01:11:48.003 --> 01:11:50.972
I don't ever talk about an open
investigation, period. Okay, Ken?


01:11:51.073 --> 01:11:53.735
Dave? Hey. Hi.


01:11:53.842 --> 01:11:56.538
Paul Avery. Can I catch a ride
with you gents when we get there?


01:11:56.645 --> 01:11:58.476
Not a good idea, Paul.


01:11:59.148 --> 01:12:01.912
He's gonna make me take a cab
when we're going to the same place.


01:12:02.017 --> 01:12:04.781
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for choosing PSA.</i>


01:12:04.887 --> 01:12:06.980
<i>- Fair enough. Fair enough.
- Please take your seats at this time.</i>


01:12:07.089 --> 01:12:09.990
<i>Remember, smoking is
in the last six aisles only.</i>


01:12:10.092 --> 01:12:11.719
<i>Enjoy your flight.</i>


01:12:15.264 --> 01:12:17.994
Cheri Jo Bates attended
Riverside Community College.


01:12:18.100 --> 01:12:22.366
She studies in the library
the night of October 30th, 1966.


01:12:22.471 --> 01:12:25.907
She leaves with an unidentified male
at closing, 9:00 p. m.


01:12:26.308 --> 01:12:30.074
Her body's found the next morning
in a parking lot, stabbed to death.


01:12:30.646 --> 01:12:33.740
<i>A typewritten confession was sent
to the Riverside Press Enterprise</i>


01:12:33.849 --> 01:12:36.477
on November 29th,
a month after Bates's murder.


01:12:36.585 --> 01:12:37.984
They ran it.


01:12:40.255 --> 01:12:42.951
"I'm not sick. I am insane.
But that will not stop the game.


01:12:43.058 --> 01:12:45.219
"This letter should be published
for all to read. "


01:12:45.327 --> 01:12:46.692
He wants to be published.
He calls it a game.


01:12:46.795 --> 01:12:48.160
I mean, this could be our boy.


01:12:48.263 --> 01:12:51.562
Six months later, the police,
the girl's father, and the paper,


01:12:51.667 --> 01:12:53.601
they all received these.


01:12:58.440 --> 01:13:00.237
Double postage, just like Zodiac.


01:13:02.044 --> 01:13:04.444
These are what Sherwood Morrill
matched to the Zodiac letters?


01:13:04.813 --> 01:13:06.644
These and the desktop. Don.


01:13:06.949 --> 01:13:11.249
This was found a couple of months later
by a janitor in RCC storage.


01:13:20.662 --> 01:13:22.823
Sherwood got
a handwriting match off wood?


01:13:24.933 --> 01:13:26.730
Who etches in their own handwriting?


01:13:27.136 --> 01:13:28.262
To be honest with you,


01:13:28.370 --> 01:13:30.736
our letters and your letters,
I don't see it.


01:13:30.839 --> 01:13:33.399
How did Paul Avery
get his hands on the exemplars?


01:13:33.509 --> 01:13:34.840
I gave them to him.


01:13:34.943 --> 01:13:36.808
We talked on the phone the other day
for about an hour.


01:13:36.912 --> 01:13:38.379
And I told him you were gonna be here.


01:13:38.480 --> 01:13:40.141
- You told him we were meeting?
- Yeah.


01:13:40.249 --> 01:13:42.444
I also told him
we don't think this is Zodiac.


01:13:42.551 --> 01:13:44.610
Okay, wait a minute.


01:13:44.720 --> 01:13:47.780
- You don't think this is Zodiac?
- We got a guy we like for it.


01:13:47.890 --> 01:13:49.448
We don't have enough
to pin it on him yet,


01:13:49.558 --> 01:13:50.786
but we're pretty sure it's him.


01:13:50.893 --> 01:13:53.760
If you don't think this is Zodiac,
then why give anything to Avery?


01:13:53.862 --> 01:13:55.489
I'm trying to cooperate.


01:13:55.597 --> 01:13:58.395
Oh, that's how you cooperate?
By giving information to reporters?


01:13:58.500 --> 01:14:00.024
Look, I don't know
about the handwriting,


01:14:00.135 --> 01:14:01.363
but Sherwood says it's a match, right?


01:14:01.470 --> 01:14:03.870
So, let's just say
that your guy did Cheri Jo.


01:14:03.972 --> 01:14:05.098
He types the confession.


01:14:05.240 --> 01:14:08.334
Zodiac reads it in the paper,
and he writes a letter taking credit for it.


01:14:08.444 --> 01:14:09.968
Now, that's something he's done before.


01:14:10.078 --> 01:14:12.672
Look, now you have everything we have.


01:14:12.781 --> 01:14:16.182
But, in my opinion,
you guys came south for nothing.


01:14:16.285 --> 01:14:18.276
FUBAR, gentlemen, FUBAR.


01:14:18.387 --> 01:14:21.117
I don't care what he says.
This still could be Z.


01:14:21.223 --> 01:14:24.420
The problem is
the entire state already thinks it is.


01:14:24.526 --> 01:14:27.859
Well, there's your press agent.
Talk to him about it.


01:14:30.399 --> 01:14:32.333
I come in peace.
I don't want any trouble.


01:14:32.434 --> 01:14:34.402
I really don't want to talk to you
right now, Paul. Not now.


01:14:34.503 --> 01:14:38.200
- Just trying to do my job.
- Oh, really? Well, now I can't do mine.


01:14:38.307 --> 01:14:40.571
We're already screwed with
the amount of tips we got on this thing,


01:14:40.974 --> 01:14:42.669
and you just freaked out the entire state.


01:14:42.776 --> 01:14:46.075
I have got Napa, Vallejo, and DOJ
looking at me sideways


01:14:46.179 --> 01:14:49.080
and Riverside's telling me
I'm on a snipe hunt!


01:14:49.182 --> 01:14:51.707
Jesus. Hey, Cheri Jo Bates was a gift.
I gave that to you.


01:14:51.818 --> 01:14:53.479
You and Armstrong
never would have found her.


01:14:53.586 --> 01:14:55.747
This may not be Zodiac.
Does that matter to you?


01:14:55.855 --> 01:14:57.288
- What if it is?
- Does it matter that Riverside may not


01:14:57.390 --> 01:14:59.358
be able to make a case
against their suspect because of you?


01:14:59.459 --> 01:15:01.359
Tell it to Sherwood.
I'm out here, beating the bushes,


01:15:01.461 --> 01:15:03.019
trying to draw him out.
We're in this together.


01:15:03.129 --> 01:15:04.494
No, we're not in anything together, Paul,


01:15:04.597 --> 01:15:06.462
because I'm not interested
in upping my circulation.


01:15:06.566 --> 01:15:09.433
Oh, boy. He wrote me.
He threatened my life.


01:15:09.536 --> 01:15:11.128
Hey, Bullitt!


01:15:11.237 --> 01:15:14.729
Been a year-and-a-half,
you gonna catch this fucking guy or not?


01:15:17.343 --> 01:15:19.709
- Go fuck yourself.
- Happily.


01:15:19.813 --> 01:15:21.804
You should have called me, Paul.


01:15:27.387 --> 01:15:28.581
Thank you.


01:15:41.634 --> 01:15:43.602
- Did you see this?
- Unfortunately, yes.


01:15:43.703 --> 01:15:46.365
Here comes every lunatic in California.


01:15:47.240 --> 01:15:48.537
I'm the Zodiac.


01:15:48.641 --> 01:15:50.199
And how did you kill your victims?


01:15:50.310 --> 01:15:52.938
With a gun. No, with a hammer.


01:15:53.046 --> 01:15:54.343
All I'm authorized to tell you


01:15:54.447 --> 01:15:56.005
is that he's still under
government employment.


01:15:56.115 --> 01:15:59.175
- And who authorized you to tell me this?
- That's all I'm authorized to say.


01:15:59.285 --> 01:16:01.480
Only a little rat bastard like Andre


01:16:01.588 --> 01:16:04.079
could have done something
like cut off all the victims' hands.


01:16:04.190 --> 01:16:06.556
Zodiac didn't cut off
any of the victims' hands.


01:16:06.659 --> 01:16:08.388
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.


01:16:08.494 --> 01:16:11.019
Travis and I worked here
side by side for 10 years.


01:16:11.130 --> 01:16:15.191
His foot gets crushed in an accident
and the killings begin.


01:16:15.301 --> 01:16:16.791
- Coincidence?
- I don't know.


01:16:16.903 --> 01:16:18.768
You're a cop, man. Do the math.


01:16:23.176 --> 01:16:26.407
Have you considered
the killer might be Paul Avery?


01:16:26.512 --> 01:16:27.774
Frequently.


01:16:28.348 --> 01:16:29.645
He was drinking Coors,
getting a load on.


01:16:30.216 --> 01:16:33.310
Starts talking about hunting people.
Like that book.


01:16:33.953 --> 01:16:36.114
Says how you can put a light
at the end of a gun


01:16:36.222 --> 01:16:37.746
to use as a sight in the dark.


01:16:37.857 --> 01:16:39.620
- He said that?
- Yeah.


01:16:40.593 --> 01:16:42.618
So I asked him,
"How would you get away with it?"


01:16:43.096 --> 01:16:44.586
And he said, "It would be easy


01:16:44.697 --> 01:16:47.131
"'cause there'd be no real motive
to the thing. "


01:16:47.233 --> 01:16:49.098
Then he said he'd write letters
to the police


01:16:49.202 --> 01:16:50.999
and call himself Zodiac
to mess with them.


01:16:51.104 --> 01:16:52.696
Leigh liked messing with people.


01:16:52.805 --> 01:16:55.797
- You're positive he said "Zodiac"?
- Yeah.


01:16:55.909 --> 01:16:59.003
I thought it was a stupid name.
So I told him.


01:16:59.112 --> 01:17:02.548
He got up all upset and said,
"I don't care what you think.


01:17:02.649 --> 01:17:05.278
"I've thought about it a long time
and that's the name I'm gonna use. "


01:17:05.385 --> 01:17:08.718
Did you feel like he'd been
thinking about it a long time?


01:17:08.821 --> 01:17:12.052
He was raw about losing his job
at the school.


01:17:12.158 --> 01:17:15.150
He talked about shooting out
the tires of a school bus


01:17:15.261 --> 01:17:17.661
and picking off the little darlings.


01:17:17.764 --> 01:17:21.825
- He actually used those words?
- That's what made me remember.


01:17:21.935 --> 01:17:24.369
Afterwards, I told my wife
I didn't wanna see him again.


01:17:24.470 --> 01:17:26.131
And I haven't since.


01:17:26.239 --> 01:17:28.799
Other thing is, Leigh's into skin diving.


01:17:28.908 --> 01:17:30.967
I know he's been up to that lake
a bunch of times.


01:17:31.077 --> 01:17:33.443
Lake Berryessa?
Did you ever go with him?


01:17:33.546 --> 01:17:37.505
Couple times. We went fishing
by Putah Creek near there.


01:17:37.617 --> 01:17:39.084
Tell him when you put it together.


01:17:39.185 --> 01:17:43.884
About a year ago, in the paper,
there was a story about the Zodiac.


01:17:43.990 --> 01:17:47.084
And it all comes back.
I tried to call the local cops.


01:17:47.193 --> 01:17:48.785
They blew him off.
Thought he was a nut.


01:17:48.895 --> 01:17:52.695
And you're sure
the conversation you had about Zodiac


01:17:52.799 --> 01:17:56.565
took place on January 1st, 1968?


01:17:56.669 --> 01:17:58.398
It couldn't have been any later.


01:17:58.504 --> 01:18:01.405
I started a new job in L.A.
on January 20th.


01:18:01.941 --> 01:18:03.408
I had to move.


01:18:03.509 --> 01:18:05.977
<i>- This is my problem. This guy...
- Arthur Leigh Allen?</i>


01:18:06.079 --> 01:18:08.673
This guy, Leigh,
just lays out his entire evil plan


01:18:08.781 --> 01:18:10.271
to a fishing buddy on New Year's Day?


01:18:10.383 --> 01:18:13.181
I don't know.
He's angry, he's been drinking,


01:18:13.286 --> 01:18:15.413
been thinking about it for a while.
I can buy that.


01:18:15.521 --> 01:18:17.853
So why didn't Cheney
contact us sooner?


01:18:17.957 --> 01:18:19.390
I checked. He did.


01:18:19.492 --> 01:18:22.484
First recorded contact
with the police department about Allen


01:18:22.595 --> 01:18:25.393
was in Pomona. January 10th, 1970.


01:18:25.498 --> 01:18:26.590
He just got lost in the shuffle.


01:18:26.699 --> 01:18:28.360
Did Cheney have anything
against Allen?


01:18:28.468 --> 01:18:29.765
Did Allen screw his wife or anything?


01:18:29.869 --> 01:18:31.564
We're gonna do
a full background check.


01:18:31.671 --> 01:18:34.333
But I got to tell you, I like this guy.


01:18:35.375 --> 01:18:37.275
So, let's pull
some handwriting samples.


01:18:39.012 --> 01:18:41.913
Hi. I talked to Sherwood.
He got the samples.


01:18:42.015 --> 01:18:43.949
- What are you having?
- BLT.


01:18:46.586 --> 01:18:49.111
So, the check stubs are a wash.
There's not enough handwriting.


01:18:49.222 --> 01:18:51.747
The application's got more,
but it doesn't look like Z's,


01:18:51.858 --> 01:18:54.156
so he can't rule him in.
But he can't rule him out, either.


01:18:54.260 --> 01:18:57.127
- Well, that's vague.
- He needs more samples.


01:18:58.197 --> 01:19:00.290
Also, our guy is a pervert.


01:19:01.367 --> 01:19:03.232
When Mel got the application
from Valley Springs,


01:19:03.336 --> 01:19:05.600
they told him that
Allen had been fired for touching kids.


01:19:05.705 --> 01:19:07.832
- Touching?
- Polite euphemism.


01:19:09.509 --> 01:19:12.637
- So what do you want to do?
- Make some phone calls.


01:19:12.745 --> 01:19:15.111
- Are you done with the fries?
- Go ahead.


01:19:15.214 --> 01:19:16.909
<i>Did you and Mr. Cheney have a chance</i>


01:19:17.016 --> 01:19:19.211
<i>to look at the copies
of the Zodiac letters we sent you?</i>


01:19:19.318 --> 01:19:22.014
Yeah.
Some of this stuff is pretty creepy.


01:19:22.121 --> 01:19:25.215
<i>- Yeah, we know that.
- I mean, creepy like Leigh.</i>


01:19:25.591 --> 01:19:28.082
He misspells words like that.
He thinks it's funny.


01:19:28.194 --> 01:19:29.991
What about the handwriting?


01:19:30.096 --> 01:19:33.031
<i>I don't know.
Don't you have experts for that stuff?</i>


01:19:33.132 --> 01:19:36.226
Our man at Questioned Documents
says it's inconclusive.


01:19:36.335 --> 01:19:38.166
Maybe he did it with his other hand.


01:19:38.271 --> 01:19:39.533
<i>The letters are a little too neat</i>


01:19:39.639 --> 01:19:42.039
<i>for someone to have written
with the wrong hand.</i>


01:19:42.141 --> 01:19:43.870
But not for Leigh, right.


01:19:43.976 --> 01:19:45.876
<i>- What do you mean?
- He's ambidextrous.</i>


01:19:45.978 --> 01:19:49.379
<i>He can write with either hand.
Didn't you guys know that?</i>


01:19:49.482 --> 01:19:52.280
In everyday life, Allen uses his left hand.


01:19:52.385 --> 01:19:54.819
Job applications,
letters to friends, et cetera.


01:19:54.921 --> 01:19:57.549
But he writes the Zodiac letters
with his right hand


01:19:57.657 --> 01:20:01.423
producing a different handwriting
that he can't be linked to.


01:20:01.894 --> 01:20:03.225
We got to see this guy, Chief.


01:20:03.329 --> 01:20:04.523
- Where is he?
- Vallejo.


01:20:04.630 --> 01:20:07.690
He works at Union Oil in Pinole.
His brother's up there, too.


01:20:07.800 --> 01:20:09.233
See them both.


01:20:09.335 --> 01:20:11.803
Make sure you call Mulanax.
It is his backyard.


01:20:11.904 --> 01:20:15.067
Oh, right, because that
worked so well for us in Riverside.


01:20:15.174 --> 01:20:17.734
Cooperation, that's us, at all costs.


01:20:27.353 --> 01:20:31.380
You can talk to him in here.
Coke machine's busted, by the way.


01:20:32.558 --> 01:20:34.492
I'll go get him for you.


01:20:35.995 --> 01:20:38.122
So how do you guys wanna do this?


01:20:38.231 --> 01:20:41.860
Well, Bill talked to the informants.
He leads, we follow?


01:20:41.968 --> 01:20:43.560
It's okay by me.


01:20:57.483 --> 01:21:00.043
Mr. Allen, I'm Inspector Bill Armstrong.


01:21:00.153 --> 01:21:03.213
This is Inspector Dave Toschi
and Sergeant Jack Mulanax.


01:21:03.322 --> 01:21:07.520
We're investigating the Zodiac murders
in San Francisco and Vallejo.


01:21:07.627 --> 01:21:09.219
Please, sit down.


01:21:18.104 --> 01:21:20.572
The informant notified us
that you made certain statements


01:21:20.673 --> 01:21:23.403
11 months prior
to the first Zodiac murder.


01:21:23.509 --> 01:21:26.444
If they're true,
they're quite incriminating.


01:21:26.546 --> 01:21:28.707
Do you recall
having any such conversation?


01:21:28.814 --> 01:21:30.111
- No.
- Have you ever read


01:21:30.216 --> 01:21:31.979
or heard anything about the Zodiac?


01:21:32.084 --> 01:21:33.312
When it was first in the paper.


01:21:33.419 --> 01:21:35.478
But I didn't follow it
after those first reports.


01:21:35.588 --> 01:21:38.989
- Why not?
- Too morbid. I...


01:21:39.091 --> 01:21:41.889
I told all this to the other officer.


01:21:41.994 --> 01:21:44.462
- Which other officer?
- From Vallejo.


01:21:45.898 --> 01:21:47.331
Do you remember his name?


01:21:47.433 --> 01:21:51.130
No, but it was right after
the murder at the lake.


01:21:51.237 --> 01:21:53.705
And what did you tell this officer?


01:21:55.308 --> 01:21:59.506
I told him that I'd gone to Salt Point
that weekend to skin dive.


01:21:59.612 --> 01:22:02.410
That I was alone
but I met a couple there.


01:22:03.616 --> 01:22:05.743
I have their names at home
if you want them.


01:22:05.851 --> 01:22:07.478
That would be great, Arthur.


01:22:07.587 --> 01:22:09.452
- Leigh.
- What?


01:22:10.356 --> 01:22:12.847
Leigh. Nobody calls me Arthur.


01:22:14.627 --> 01:22:18.028
Also, that day when I came home,
my neighbor saw me.


01:22:18.130 --> 01:22:21.896
It was around 4:00.
But I forgot to tell the other officer that.


01:22:22.001 --> 01:22:24.162
- Neighbor's name?
- Bill White.


01:22:26.005 --> 01:22:27.768
He died a week or so afterwards.


01:22:27.873 --> 01:22:30.842
Heart attack.
So I didn't think to call to follow up.


01:22:33.446 --> 01:22:35.539
The knives I had in my car
with the blood on them,


01:22:35.648 --> 01:22:39.175
that blood came from a chicken
that I killed for dinner.


01:22:41.988 --> 01:22:44.786
- What?
- I had knives in my car that weekend.


01:22:44.890 --> 01:22:49.156
Maybe Bill saw them
and called the other officer on me.


01:22:49.795 --> 01:22:52.491
Well, we'll be checking in on that.


01:22:52.598 --> 01:22:54.395
Well, let me ask you something else.


01:22:54.500 --> 01:22:58.834
Were you ever in Southern California
at any time in 1966?


01:22:59.472 --> 01:23:01.963
- Is this about the Riverside killing?
- Yes.


01:23:03.109 --> 01:23:05.339
Well, I guess I was there
around that time.


01:23:05.444 --> 01:23:08.777
I used to go down there a lot.
I like the auto races.


01:23:13.119 --> 01:23:15.553
Informant says that
you're ambidextrous?


01:23:15.655 --> 01:23:17.589
No, that's untrue.


01:23:17.690 --> 01:23:19.988
You can't write with both hands?


01:23:21.160 --> 01:23:24.220
My teachers tried to make me
when I was a kid, but I couldn't.


01:23:24.330 --> 01:23:26.423
I'm left-handed.


01:23:26.532 --> 01:23:30.696
He also said that you made statements
about killing school children.


01:23:31.404 --> 01:23:32.894
That is...


01:23:33.005 --> 01:23:36.270
That is horrible. That is...
That's a horrible thing to say.


01:23:36.375 --> 01:23:39.708
So, you weren't angry
about being fired from Valley Springs


01:23:39.812 --> 01:23:41.871
for touching your students?


01:23:51.157 --> 01:23:52.852
I'm not the Zodiac.


01:23:53.826 --> 01:23:56.693
And if I was, I certainly wouldn't tell you.


01:23:59.065 --> 01:24:00.862
That's a nice watch.


01:24:02.735 --> 01:24:03.724
Thank you.


01:24:03.836 --> 01:24:05.269
May I see it?


01:24:07.206 --> 01:24:08.639
May I see it?


01:24:20.453 --> 01:24:21.545
Where'd you get it?


01:24:21.954 --> 01:24:23.922
It was a Christmas gift
from my mother two years ago.


01:24:24.590 --> 01:24:26.717
That's very sweet.


01:24:26.826 --> 01:24:29.317
So, tell me something, Arthur.


01:24:29.428 --> 01:24:30.554
You don't remember anyone


01:24:30.663 --> 01:24:34.190
you might have had a conversation with
regarding the Zodiac?


01:24:35.668 --> 01:24:41.072
Maybe Ted Kidder or Phil Tucker
at Vallejo Recreation.


01:24:42.375 --> 01:24:44.206
But I couldn't be positive.


01:24:44.310 --> 01:24:46.175
I used to work there when...


01:24:50.116 --> 01:24:52.175
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.</i>


01:24:53.486 --> 01:24:54.578
What?


01:24:54.687 --> 01:24:57.850
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.
That's why you're here, isn't it?</i>


01:24:57.957 --> 01:24:59.686
It was my favorite book in high school.


01:24:59.792 --> 01:25:03.250
It's about this man who waits for people
to get shipwrecked on this island.


01:25:03.362 --> 01:25:04.761
Because he was
tired of hunting animals,


01:25:04.864 --> 01:25:06.456
he hunted the people for the challenge.


01:25:06.565 --> 01:25:10.695
And man is the most
dangerous animal of all?


01:25:10.803 --> 01:25:13.294
That's the whole point of the story.


01:25:14.006 --> 01:25:15.337
Great book.


01:25:16.575 --> 01:25:19.203
Or, at least, that's what I told Phil.


01:25:24.884 --> 01:25:26.112
May I go?


01:25:29.755 --> 01:25:30.813
Sure.


01:25:35.628 --> 01:25:39.894
- Thanks for your time.
- I'm willing to help in any way possible.


01:25:39.999 --> 01:25:42.058
I look forward to the day


01:25:42.168 --> 01:25:45.626
when police officers
are no longer referred to as pigs.


01:25:46.639 --> 01:25:47.799
Thanks.


01:25:48.941 --> 01:25:50.568
We'll be in touch.


01:26:02.354 --> 01:26:06.222
So does anyone think this suspect
warrants further investigation?


01:26:06.325 --> 01:26:09.590
These are copies of some
of the Zodiac letters that were sent.


01:26:10.329 --> 01:26:13.230
We'd like you to take a look at them.


01:26:13.466 --> 01:26:15.331
You think my brother's the Zodiac.


01:26:15.434 --> 01:26:17.402
Well, we're looking at him.


01:26:17.503 --> 01:26:18.868
Are you going to arrest him?


01:26:18.971 --> 01:26:22.907
Mrs. Allen, we don't arrest people
just because we're interested in them.


01:26:23.008 --> 01:26:24.441
Well, Leigh's always been troubled.


01:26:24.543 --> 01:26:26.738
Is it true about the children?


01:26:27.446 --> 01:26:28.743
Unfortunately.


01:26:28.848 --> 01:26:31.510
We don't see him much anymore
since we found out.


01:26:31.617 --> 01:26:33.585
What are your feelings
about Don Cheney?


01:26:33.686 --> 01:26:36.086
Don Cheney? My old roommate?


01:26:36.188 --> 01:26:39.055
- Was he the one who contacted you?
- That's confidential.


01:26:39.158 --> 01:26:40.682
Well, Don's a very reliable guy.


01:26:40.793 --> 01:26:43.853
If he were to tell you something,
I'd believe it to be true.


01:26:43.963 --> 01:26:45.123
- This one.
- What about it?


01:26:45.231 --> 01:26:47.222
Here, where he spells
"Christmas" with two "S's. "


01:26:47.333 --> 01:26:49.631
We got a Christmas card from Leigh
a couple years ago.


01:26:49.835 --> 01:26:52.531
He spelled it the exact same way.
Christ-mass.


01:26:52.638 --> 01:26:55.072
- Would you still have that?
- I can look for it.


01:26:55.474 --> 01:26:57.567
Thank you. That'd be great.


01:26:58.711 --> 01:27:00.736
Is there anything else
we can do to help?


01:27:00.846 --> 01:27:02.473
<i>The brother said
he would search Leigh's apartment</i>


01:27:02.581 --> 01:27:03.809
next time he went out of town.


01:27:03.916 --> 01:27:06.146
- That gets you around a warrant.
- For the time being.


01:27:06.252 --> 01:27:09.483
If we do find something,
Mulanax will go to the DA in Vallejo,


01:27:09.588 --> 01:27:11.317
and we could search the place properly.


01:27:11.423 --> 01:27:12.890
Now I got a chance to talk to the cop


01:27:12.992 --> 01:27:15.859
who interviewed Leigh Allen
two days after the Berryessa murders.


01:27:15.961 --> 01:27:17.656
Doesn't remember how he got onto him,


01:27:17.763 --> 01:27:20.755
but didn't think he looked like a killer
so he didn't like him for Z.


01:27:20.866 --> 01:27:23.699
- But you do?
- I wish I could've taken the guy in there.


01:27:23.802 --> 01:27:26.737
Take it slow, Dave.
Try and find more stuff for Sherwood.


01:27:26.839 --> 01:27:28.864
A match'll get us farther
on the warrants.


01:27:28.974 --> 01:27:32.068
- Avery's on two.
- Tell him to screw.


01:27:32.177 --> 01:27:36.477
You want me to communicate that
verbatim or can I spice it up a little?


01:27:43.819 --> 01:27:46.151
This suspect is not your Zodiac.


01:27:48.157 --> 01:27:50.785
This sample matches the canceled
checks and the application?


01:27:50.893 --> 01:27:51.882
Perfectly.


01:27:51.994 --> 01:27:55.191
So we've just retested the left hand.
I mean, we know he's ambidextrous.


01:27:55.297 --> 01:27:58.528
In 38 years, I've never seen anyone
that ambidextrous.


01:27:58.634 --> 01:28:01.125
Both hands would have commonalities.


01:28:01.503 --> 01:28:02.765
I'm sorry.


01:28:03.272 --> 01:28:05.001
Just not gonna work.


01:28:06.942 --> 01:28:09.342
<i>- Homicide, Toschi.
- Dave, it's Jack Mulanax.</i>


01:28:09.445 --> 01:28:11.572
Hey. Mulanax. Yeah.


01:28:11.680 --> 01:28:13.079
<i>We struck out with the judge.</i>


01:28:13.182 --> 01:28:14.809
<i>He won't sign off on a warrant
for Allen's house.</i>


01:28:14.917 --> 01:28:16.942
- Why not?
- Said it wasn't enough.


01:28:17.052 --> 01:28:19.384
Now, unless we bring him a handwriting
match or some evidence that...


01:28:19.488 --> 01:28:21.854
How are we gonna get evidence
if we can't toss the house?


01:28:21.957 --> 01:28:23.390
<i>I don't know.</i>


01:28:23.959 --> 01:28:26.860
<i>- I truly am sorry.
- No, no. Thank you, Jack.</i>


01:28:28.764 --> 01:28:29.822
What do you wanna do?


01:28:29.932 --> 01:28:31.263
Don't know what I can do
without Vallejo.


01:28:31.366 --> 01:28:34.199
We need Allen's right hand.
We can't get it without a warrant.


01:28:34.303 --> 01:28:36.396
Are there other guys
you should be looking at?


01:28:36.505 --> 01:28:38.439
Only, what?


01:28:38.540 --> 01:28:40.440
Twenty-three hundred?


01:28:40.542 --> 01:28:41.873
Okay, then.


01:28:45.047 --> 01:28:46.378
Okay, then.


01:29:14.309 --> 01:29:16.971
Paul, you wrote the Justice Department


01:29:17.079 --> 01:29:20.412
asking to be put in charge
of the Zodiac investigation?


01:29:22.451 --> 01:29:24.351
I merely suggested...


01:29:24.453 --> 01:29:25.647
On our letterhead?


01:29:25.754 --> 01:29:27.779
...that those with intimate knowledge
of the case


01:29:27.890 --> 01:29:29.824
create an information clearinghouse


01:29:29.925 --> 01:29:32.052
to promote an exchange
and free flow of ideas.


01:29:32.160 --> 01:29:35.220
- And that you run it.
- Well, who better than me?


01:29:36.298 --> 01:29:37.822
The marked man.


01:29:38.534 --> 01:29:40.502
Paul, if you want to work here,
I need three things.


01:29:40.602 --> 01:29:42.069
One, stop boozing.


01:29:42.170 --> 01:29:45.333
Two, stop doing
whatever else it is you're doing.


01:29:45.440 --> 01:29:48.932
And three, cut this nonsense out.


01:29:49.044 --> 01:29:52.104
Sweetest of Templetons, if at any time


01:29:52.214 --> 01:29:57.413
you feel my excellent work is no longer
in step with this trashy provincial rag,


01:29:57.519 --> 01:29:59.180
I'll more than happily...


01:29:59.288 --> 01:30:02.746
More than happily
decamp for greener pastures.


01:30:02.858 --> 01:30:04.189
Paul, I mean it!


01:30:14.670 --> 01:30:16.535
- Paul?
- Yep.


01:30:16.638 --> 01:30:19.835
- What was that?
- An editorial tête-à-tête.


01:30:20.976 --> 01:30:23.103
- Wanna grab a drink?
- It's 10:00 in the morning.


01:30:23.211 --> 01:30:25.008
Late breakfast?


01:30:26.048 --> 01:30:28.141
- Early lunch, or...
- Paul.


01:30:30.652 --> 01:30:32.085
Are you okay?


01:30:32.955 --> 01:30:33.979
No.


01:30:37.426 --> 01:30:39.223
Thank you for asking.


01:30:41.463 --> 01:30:43.590
Shorty! Let's go out for one.


01:30:43.699 --> 01:30:45.690
Paul, where are you going?


01:30:47.769 --> 01:30:50.237
<i>So, you moved off my brother-in-law?</i>


01:30:50.339 --> 01:30:52.364
We couldn't get a warrant.


01:30:53.942 --> 01:30:57.469
Last year we arranged for Leigh
to get help from a social worker.


01:30:57.579 --> 01:30:59.137
He only went twice.


01:30:59.247 --> 01:31:02.216
We saw him recently for
the first time in nine months.


01:31:02.317 --> 01:31:05.377
My mother-in-law brought him by
to see the new baby.


01:31:05.487 --> 01:31:08.786
After he left,
I went to see that social worker.


01:31:08.890 --> 01:31:12.223
He couldn't talk about a former patient,
so I just asked him straight out


01:31:12.327 --> 01:31:14.488
if he thought Leigh
was capable of killing people.


01:31:14.596 --> 01:31:17.827
- Because of patient confidentiality...
- The man said yes.


01:31:19.668 --> 01:31:21.829
Why hadn't you seen him
in nine months?


01:31:21.937 --> 01:31:23.837
He's going to school in Santa Rosa.


01:31:23.939 --> 01:31:27.272
- Santa Rosa? Where is he living?
- In his trailer.


01:31:27.376 --> 01:31:29.401
- In Santa Rosa?
- Sonoma County.


01:31:29.511 --> 01:31:31.706
We wouldn't have to go
through the Vallejo DA.


01:31:31.813 --> 01:31:33.303
It's been 11 months
since you talked to this guy,


01:31:33.415 --> 01:31:34.939
and now you wanna search his trailer?


01:31:35.050 --> 01:31:36.813
If we find something, great.


01:31:36.918 --> 01:31:40.081
If not, we get his prints and
handwriting samples from both hands.


01:31:40.188 --> 01:31:42.554
I thought Sherwood shut you down.


01:31:43.291 --> 01:31:45.759
What if I can get a second opinion?


01:31:46.928 --> 01:31:49.158
I don't wanna step on Sherwood's toes.
He trained me at this.


01:31:49.264 --> 01:31:51.789
Terry, all I need to know
is if the suspect is ambidextrous.


01:31:51.900 --> 01:31:55.859
Could he possibly have written
those letters with his other hand?


01:31:57.572 --> 01:31:58.937
Between you and me?


01:31:59.041 --> 01:32:02.477
Because there are differing
schools of thought on this.


01:32:03.679 --> 01:32:08.116
Get the samples of his other hand.
If he's the Zodiac, you'll get a match.


01:32:08.216 --> 01:32:10.776
<i>That's the current thinking,
according to Terry Pascoe.</i>


01:32:10.886 --> 01:32:14.151
Meanwhile, I spoke to a psychologist
who'd be willing to testify


01:32:14.256 --> 01:32:17.225
that someone who undergoes
a personality change like Zodiac


01:32:17.325 --> 01:32:20.260
would manifest it physically,
altering his handwriting.


01:32:20.362 --> 01:32:23.957
Which is why Sherwood couldn't
get a match from Allen's samples.


01:32:24.066 --> 01:32:26.296
We got Terry Pascoe,
this psychology guy,


01:32:26.401 --> 01:32:27.732
coupled with Cheney...


01:32:27.836 --> 01:32:29.303
It could be enough for a warrant.


01:32:29.404 --> 01:32:30.530
Get Cheney on the record.


01:32:30.639 --> 01:32:33.199
"And shoot the kiddies
as they came bouncing out.


01:32:33.308 --> 01:32:36.368
"And that he would call himself Zodiac. "


01:32:37.379 --> 01:32:38.403
Yes.


01:32:38.513 --> 01:32:42.074
And you're willing to swear
to this, under oath, in Superior Court?


01:32:42.184 --> 01:32:43.583
Without any hesitation.


01:32:43.685 --> 01:32:46.415
Thank you very much, Mr. Cheney.
Thank you very much for your time.


01:32:46.521 --> 01:32:47.852
Thank you.


01:32:49.357 --> 01:32:52.087
Well, looks like you got your man.


01:33:12.748 --> 01:33:14.010
Mr. Allen?


01:33:14.116 --> 01:33:16.016
This is the
Santa Rosa Police Department.


01:33:16.118 --> 01:33:18.916
We have a warrant
to search your residence.


01:33:29.998 --> 01:33:31.124
Hello?


01:33:39.775 --> 01:33:42.005
I'll check with the neighbors.


01:33:43.445 --> 01:33:44.434
Close the door.


01:33:44.546 --> 01:33:47.572
Close the door,
there's rodents running around.


01:33:59.928 --> 01:34:02.453
Neighbor said he tore out of here
about a half-hour ago.


01:34:02.564 --> 01:34:06.398
- You think somebody tipped him?
- We're not leaving till he comes back.


01:34:12.707 --> 01:34:14.436
I'll check the back.


01:34:27.189 --> 01:34:28.281
Jesus.


01:34:28.390 --> 01:34:29.982
- What?
- Squirrels.


01:34:32.160 --> 01:34:34.094
Piece of work, this guy.


01:34:40.902 --> 01:34:43.702
Not one, but two blue windbreakers.


01:34:43.805 --> 01:34:47.468
- Like the Stine scene?
- We'll have those checked for blood.


01:34:47.909 --> 01:34:50.810
And a pair of black gloves.


01:34:52.080 --> 01:34:55.379
Men's seven,
just like the ones we found in the cab.


01:34:55.483 --> 01:34:58.145
Well, he's got the same size shoes
and gloves as Z.


01:34:58.253 --> 01:35:00.483
Probably just a coincidence.


01:35:00.589 --> 01:35:04.423
Dave, I got a gun.
Check that. Two guns.


01:35:05.894 --> 01:35:09.057
They're both.22s.
One automatic, one revolver.


01:35:09.164 --> 01:35:10.654
Well, that's interesting.


01:35:10.765 --> 01:35:13.893
Because he happens to have
an M-1 rifle here in the closet.


01:35:14.002 --> 01:35:16.596
For little darlings bouncing off buses.


01:35:17.939 --> 01:35:19.429
Someone's here.


01:35:26.581 --> 01:35:28.981
Hello, Arthur. Remember us?


01:35:51.573 --> 01:35:52.562
No.


01:35:52.674 --> 01:35:53.732
On the handwriting?


01:35:53.842 --> 01:35:57.334
Ballistics, no match.
Prints, no match. Writing, no match.


01:35:57.445 --> 01:35:59.242
On both hands, right?


01:35:59.347 --> 01:36:01.144
Because we got handwriting
from both his hands.


01:36:01.249 --> 01:36:02.580
And neither hand matches.


01:36:02.684 --> 01:36:04.311
Forget Sherwood.
Let's get another opinion.


01:36:04.419 --> 01:36:06.410
Fellas, he's not your guy.


01:36:12.894 --> 01:36:14.088
Damn it.


01:36:21.403 --> 01:36:22.427
Hey.


01:36:23.405 --> 01:36:25.839
What do you want? Time off?


01:36:28.109 --> 01:36:29.235
A hug?


01:36:30.111 --> 01:36:32.136
Do you know what
the worst part of this is?


01:36:32.247 --> 01:36:34.147
I can't tell if I wanted it
to be Allen so bad


01:36:34.249 --> 01:36:37.514
because I actually thought it was him,
or I just want all this to be over.


01:36:37.619 --> 01:36:39.519
It's because you thought it was him.


01:36:39.621 --> 01:36:41.111
And I did, too.


01:36:43.892 --> 01:36:45.325
You know what? Take some time off.


01:36:45.427 --> 01:36:48.726
Spend some time with your wife
and the kids.


01:36:48.830 --> 01:36:51.355
Go to Candlestick. See a movie.


01:36:52.701 --> 01:36:57.468
<i>"To the city of San Francisco,
I will enjoy killing one person every day</i>


01:36:58.106 --> 01:37:00.506
<i>"until you pay me $100,000.</i>


01:37:01.409 --> 01:37:04.105
<i>"If you agree, say so tomorrow morning</i>


01:37:04.846 --> 01:37:07.974
<i>"in the personal column
San Francisco Chronicle,</i>


01:37:08.083 --> 01:37:10.051
<i>"and I will set up meeting.</i>


01:37:10.151 --> 01:37:11.743
<i>"If I do not hear from you,</i>


01:37:11.853 --> 01:37:15.186
<i>"it will be my next pleasure
to kill a Catholic priest or a...</i>


01:37:18.259 --> 01:37:19.590
<i>"... Scorpio. "</i>


01:37:22.097 --> 01:37:23.564
<i>Who's out of their minds?</i>


01:37:23.665 --> 01:37:25.724
I've got to get out of here.


01:37:25.834 --> 01:37:29.099
<i>Where the hell does he expect me
to find $100,000?</i>


01:37:29.204 --> 01:37:31.570
<i>You're not thinking of paying him,
are you, Mr. Mayor?</i>


01:37:31.673 --> 01:37:35.973
<i>The city of San Francisco does not
pay criminals not to commit a crime.</i>


01:37:58.900 --> 01:38:01.368
The killer gets shot in the chest.


01:38:01.469 --> 01:38:03.733
That's how it ends.


01:38:04.205 --> 01:38:05.365
Do I know you?


01:38:05.473 --> 01:38:08.670
<i>I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the Chronicle with Paul Avery.</i>


01:38:08.777 --> 01:38:10.335
Dave Toschi. Nice to meet you.


01:38:10.445 --> 01:38:12.936
Dave! That Harry Callahan
did a hell of a job with your case.


01:38:13.048 --> 01:38:15.642
Yeah. No need for due process, right?


01:38:19.988 --> 01:38:22.183
<i>- What do you do at the Chronicle?
- I'm a cartoonist.</i>


01:38:22.290 --> 01:38:23.382
That's nice.


01:38:23.491 --> 01:38:25.391
You're gonna catch him.


01:38:27.062 --> 01:38:29.860
Pal, they're already
making movies about it.


01:39:01.563 --> 01:39:03.724
Hi. We haven't met.


01:39:03.832 --> 01:39:05.663
I'm Robert Graysmith.


01:39:05.767 --> 01:39:07.701
I'm Duffy Jennings.


01:39:07.802 --> 01:39:10.862
- Nice to meet you.
- Good to meet you, man.


01:39:10.972 --> 01:39:12.200
You got a great desk.


01:39:12.307 --> 01:39:14.332
Guy who used to work here
was a great reporter.


01:39:14.442 --> 01:39:15.704
Oh, yeah. Oh, I'm sure he was.


01:39:15.810 --> 01:39:18.278
<i>I mean, it's a honor
to leave the Chronicle</i>


01:39:18.379 --> 01:39:21.177
<i>and go work for the Sacramento Bee.</i>


01:39:21.282 --> 01:39:23.443
Dare to dream, right, Robert?


01:39:27.055 --> 01:39:29.990
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you, too.


01:39:30.091 --> 01:39:32.184
I'm just right down there
at the Art department


01:39:32.293 --> 01:39:34.761
- if you need anything, Duffy.
- Yeah.


01:39:38.233 --> 01:39:40.963
- You sure you don't want the car, Bill?
- It's your turn.


01:39:41.069 --> 01:39:44.232
You could just drop me off at my place
and take the car.


01:39:44.339 --> 01:39:46.273
You should keep the car.


01:39:47.041 --> 01:39:48.099
Yeah?


01:39:48.576 --> 01:39:50.635
I'm not coming in tomorrow.


01:39:52.614 --> 01:39:54.104
Why? What's up?


01:39:55.283 --> 01:39:56.511
I'm done.


01:39:58.119 --> 01:40:00.053
I put in for a transfer.


01:40:05.927 --> 01:40:07.155
Where?


01:40:07.795 --> 01:40:09.387
Looking at Fraud.


01:40:11.699 --> 01:40:13.758
I can't be on call anymore.


01:40:16.471 --> 01:40:18.735
I wanna see these kids grow up.


01:40:19.941 --> 01:40:22.171
Hey, good for you, Bill.


01:40:24.078 --> 01:40:26.569
- You'll be okay.
- Yeah. I'll be fine.


01:40:28.716 --> 01:40:29.740
Hey,


01:40:30.752 --> 01:40:34.153
I'm not leaving you
holding the bag on anything, am I?


01:40:35.857 --> 01:40:36.881
No.


01:40:39.260 --> 01:40:40.318
Okay.


01:40:41.029 --> 01:40:42.724
Hey, you know what?


01:40:43.398 --> 01:40:47.164
Maybe you'll have a chance
to try your Japanese food, the raw stuff.


01:40:48.503 --> 01:40:49.561
Yeah.


01:41:21.703 --> 01:41:23.398
I'm not Paul Avery.


01:41:26.074 --> 01:41:29.237
The boys need to be tucked in, please,
and the baby needs changing.


01:41:29.344 --> 01:41:31.642
- I'll flip you for it.
- You wish.


01:41:35.116 --> 01:41:37.778
Nobody has more Zodiac crap
than you do.


01:42:22.430 --> 01:42:24.625
- Are you kidding me?
- Hi, Paul.


01:42:26.434 --> 01:42:28.834
- Permission to come aboard.
- It's right there.


01:42:28.936 --> 01:42:31.700
Anyway, you got shoes on.
This is perfect right here.


01:42:31.806 --> 01:42:33.706
- That's the one.
- Okay.


01:42:35.376 --> 01:42:38.243
- See that? Mesmerizing.
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.


01:42:38.346 --> 01:42:40.974
My own kids
would kill me for one of those.


01:42:42.850 --> 01:42:45.080
- How are you?
- Fantastic.


01:42:45.186 --> 01:42:47.313
I mean, admittedly,


01:42:47.422 --> 01:42:49.686
<i>the Bee ain't exactly
the Chron, but fuck it, right?</i>


01:42:49.791 --> 01:42:52.760
Do you want a drink?
I don't have anything blue, but I got...


01:42:52.860 --> 01:42:54.828
Don't worry about that.
Don't worry about it.


01:42:54.929 --> 01:42:58.490
It's no bother at all.
Nobody comes by from the old days.


01:42:58.900 --> 01:42:59.924
Cheers.


01:43:00.702 --> 01:43:02.829
To your health and mine.


01:43:04.739 --> 01:43:06.104
Mostly mine.


01:43:11.346 --> 01:43:12.836
So,


01:43:14.949 --> 01:43:16.280
what's new?


01:43:18.319 --> 01:43:20.219
- I've been thinking.
- Yeah.


01:43:20.321 --> 01:43:21.549
Somebody should write a book.


01:43:21.656 --> 01:43:24.591
Somebody should write a fucking book,
that's for sure.


01:43:24.692 --> 01:43:26.819
- About what?
- About Zodiac.


01:43:28.463 --> 01:43:29.862
It's not new.


01:43:29.964 --> 01:43:34.594
I've been thinking that
if you put all the information together,


01:43:34.702 --> 01:43:36.260
maybe you could jog something loose.


01:43:36.371 --> 01:43:38.862
And then I was thinking that
nobody knows the case better than you.


01:43:38.973 --> 01:43:39.997
Yeah. That's true.


01:43:40.108 --> 01:43:43.100
You know all the players,
and you have all the files.


01:43:43.211 --> 01:43:44.508
Lost them.


01:43:44.846 --> 01:43:45.904
You lost them?


01:43:46.013 --> 01:43:49.278
Or I tossed them. I don't know.
I moved onto a boat.


01:43:49.717 --> 01:43:51.776
You know that we work
in the daily business, right?


01:43:51.886 --> 01:43:53.148
As in, today.


01:43:53.254 --> 01:43:56.018
What do you think
we were doing back then?


01:43:57.024 --> 01:43:59.151
Do you know that more people die
in the East Bay commute


01:43:59.260 --> 01:44:01.558
every three months
than that idiot ever killed?


01:44:01.662 --> 01:44:02.822
He offed a few citizens,


01:44:02.930 --> 01:44:06.266
he wrote a few letters,
and he faded into a footnote.


01:44:11.773 --> 01:44:14.765
Not that I haven't been sitting here idly


01:44:14.876 --> 01:44:18.835
waiting for you to drop by
and reinvigorate my sense of purpose.


01:44:21.182 --> 01:44:24.310
It was four years ago. Let it fucking go.


01:44:24.419 --> 01:44:27.115
You're wrong. It was important.


01:44:28.389 --> 01:44:30.880
Then, what did you ever do about it?


01:44:31.759 --> 01:44:33.886
If it was so fucking important,
what did you ever do?


01:44:33.995 --> 01:44:36.828
You hovered over my desk,
you stole from wastebaskets.


01:44:36.931 --> 01:44:38.558
Am I being unkind?


01:44:39.734 --> 01:44:42.999
Oh, that's right, I forgot.
You went to the library.


01:44:45.807 --> 01:44:47.775
I'm sorry I bothered you.


01:45:09.897 --> 01:45:11.922
- Hey, hi.
- Hi.


01:45:12.033 --> 01:45:14.467
- Where you been?
- The library.


01:45:46.133 --> 01:45:47.430
Thank you!


01:46:03.184 --> 01:46:06.551
- Inspector Toschi?
- Yeah? One moment, please.


01:46:10.925 --> 01:46:12.119
- Hi.
- Hi.


01:46:13.427 --> 01:46:15.418
We met at the movies once.


01:46:15.930 --> 01:46:17.295
It must have been magical.


01:46:17.398 --> 01:46:19.127
<i>I'm Robert Graysmith.
I work at the Chronicle.</i>


01:46:19.233 --> 01:46:21.997
I was wondering if I could buy you lunch.


01:46:23.738 --> 01:46:25.399
Sure, why not?


01:46:25.506 --> 01:46:27.872
So, you're a friend of Paul Avery's?


01:46:27.975 --> 01:46:30.375
He's actually the reason I'm here.


01:46:32.113 --> 01:46:34.479
I wanted to ask you about Zodiac.


01:46:34.949 --> 01:46:38.180
Well, I appreciate the interest,
but we don't discuss open cases.


01:46:38.286 --> 01:46:40.811
Oh, well, what's going on with it,
day to day?


01:46:40.922 --> 01:46:42.583
We're actively pursuing all leads.


01:46:42.690 --> 01:46:45.250
And you're the only one on it, right?


01:46:46.427 --> 01:46:47.894
Mr. Graysmith,


01:46:49.030 --> 01:46:50.998
Zodiac hasn't written in three years.


01:46:51.098 --> 01:46:53.828
You know how many murders
we've had in San Francisco since then?


01:46:53.935 --> 01:46:55.425
- No.
- Over 200.


01:46:55.536 --> 01:46:58.835
That's a lot of dead people
and grieving families that need our help.


01:46:58.940 --> 01:47:00.532
So, nobody cares.


01:47:00.675 --> 01:47:03.109
Excuse me? I care.


01:47:05.813 --> 01:47:08.077
Okay. Can I show you something?


01:47:10.985 --> 01:47:14.148
I've been doing research
on the first cipher.


01:47:14.255 --> 01:47:16.018
Everything an amateur
would need to create it


01:47:16.123 --> 01:47:19.092
can be found in these books.


01:47:19.193 --> 01:47:22.526
Now, I started thinking
that if you can track these books,


01:47:22.630 --> 01:47:25.030
then maybe you can track the man.


01:47:25.566 --> 01:47:28.399
So, I remember you thought
that Zodiac was military,


01:47:28.502 --> 01:47:32.165
so I went to every base library
and I got a list of every person


01:47:32.273 --> 01:47:36.209
who's ever checked out these books
and that's when I found this.


01:47:40.948 --> 01:47:43.439
- Missing.
- It means they were stolen.


01:47:44.251 --> 01:47:47.812
So, almost every book on ciphers
was stolen from the Presidio Library?


01:47:47.922 --> 01:47:50.516
And the Oakland Army Terminal Library.


01:47:53.327 --> 01:47:57.764
Somebody didn't want a record
of ever having checked out these books.


01:47:57.865 --> 01:47:59.492
Who are you again?


01:48:01.602 --> 01:48:03.229
I just wanna help.


01:48:06.440 --> 01:48:08.704
I can't allow you to help.


01:48:08.809 --> 01:48:10.572
I can't discuss the case with you.


01:48:10.678 --> 01:48:13.112
I can't give you information,
and I certainly couldn't tell you


01:48:13.214 --> 01:48:15.409
to go see Ken Narlow in Napa.


01:48:15.983 --> 01:48:17.348
N- A-R-L-O-W.


01:48:27.361 --> 01:48:32.025
I'm sorry, Mr. Graysmith,
but we don't cooperate with writers.


01:48:32.133 --> 01:48:34.897
Well, I'm not a writer, I'm a cartoonist.


01:48:35.836 --> 01:48:38.031
- And Dave Toschi sent you?
- Yes.


01:48:38.139 --> 01:48:40.107
- Why?
- Maybe he...


01:48:40.207 --> 01:48:43.005
Maybe he thought
that I could do some good.


01:48:43.744 --> 01:48:47.908
- What are you, some kind of boy scout?
- Eagle Scout, actually, first class.


01:48:48.883 --> 01:48:52.046
Well, if you wanna do this,
don't let me stop you.


01:48:53.187 --> 01:48:55.678
Better start with Vallejo, Jack Mulanax.


01:48:56.257 --> 01:48:58.122
I understand what you're trying to do.


01:48:58.893 --> 01:49:01.088
But this is an open police investigation.


01:49:01.195 --> 01:49:03.288
I'm a friend of Dave Toschi's.


01:49:03.397 --> 01:49:06.662
And he said
that you might be able to help.


01:49:06.767 --> 01:49:09.668
I mean, the case is dead.
Zodiac's long gone.


01:49:10.604 --> 01:49:12.765
He's yesterday's news, right?


01:49:13.841 --> 01:49:15.604
That's what they say.


01:49:16.544 --> 01:49:18.375
So, what's the harm?


01:49:18.479 --> 01:49:19.912
<i>No pens, no paper.</i>


01:49:20.481 --> 01:49:23.143
Anything that you see that's relevant,
you got to remember in your head.


01:49:23.250 --> 01:49:24.308
Okay.


01:49:26.554 --> 01:49:27.851
Okay, here we go.


01:49:27.955 --> 01:49:30.014
- Which one?
- All of them.


01:49:30.124 --> 01:49:32.820
And there's more in the next room.
They're all marked with these numbers.


01:49:32.927 --> 01:49:34.121
243-146.


01:49:34.228 --> 01:49:36.059
You don't smoke, do you?


01:49:36.163 --> 01:49:38.256
Once. In high school.


01:49:41.669 --> 01:49:43.034
What's this?


01:49:43.971 --> 01:49:45.268
Thank you.


01:50:13.501 --> 01:50:15.492
<i>Man, you really creeped us out.</i>


01:50:21.275 --> 01:50:22.674
<i>"Nine millimeter.</i>


01:50:24.945 --> 01:50:27.470
<i>"Said nothing and began firing. "</i>


01:50:36.290 --> 01:50:37.587
"Most Dangerous Game.


01:50:37.691 --> 01:50:40.455
<i>"Do not eliminate this suspect
because of handwriting.</i>


01:50:40.561 --> 01:50:42.654
<i>"Not because of handwriting.</i>


01:50:43.230 --> 01:50:45.198
"Darlene's sister, Linda.


01:50:45.299 --> 01:50:47.961
"It was all just deep breathing. George.


01:50:48.602 --> 01:50:51.366
"It was a strange man. George.
Strange man. "


01:50:52.339 --> 01:50:53.966
Thank you so much.


01:50:55.876 --> 01:50:57.867
Oh, briefcase. Oh, thanks.


01:51:00.581 --> 01:51:03.106
- Hey, Jack.
- Hey, Bawart.


01:51:03.217 --> 01:51:05.048
- Who's that?
- That's Graysmith.


01:51:05.152 --> 01:51:08.417
Some cartoonist.
Thinks he's gonna solve the Zodiac.


01:51:10.090 --> 01:51:11.387
Well, good for him.


01:51:41.889 --> 01:51:44.153
- Thank you for meeting me, Inspector.
- No. We're not meeting, Robert.


01:51:44.258 --> 01:51:45.782
We're just two guys
who happen to be sitting


01:51:45.893 --> 01:51:47.053
on the same bench at the same time.


01:51:47.161 --> 01:51:49.561
I've got five minutes.
I've got to get back to the Hall.


01:51:49.663 --> 01:51:52.393
Okay. As far as you know,
did anyone ever get in touch


01:51:52.499 --> 01:51:54.194
with Mike Mageau
during your investigation


01:51:54.301 --> 01:51:56.769
- and show him suspect photos?
- Why?


01:51:56.871 --> 01:51:59.305
Well, he's the only surviving victim
who ever saw Zodiac without a mask.


01:51:59.406 --> 01:52:00.737
No, I mean, why are you asking me?


01:52:00.841 --> 01:52:02.703
Mageau and Darlene,
that's Vallejo's case.


01:52:02.810 --> 01:52:05.574
Paul Stine is mine.
You've got four minutes now.


01:52:05.679 --> 01:52:07.772
Darlene Ferrin was being followed.


01:52:07.882 --> 01:52:09.850
Now, I know Mulanax says
that they already found this guy,


01:52:09.950 --> 01:52:10.939
a George Waters?


01:52:11.051 --> 01:52:12.848
But he also said
that she had a lot of admirers


01:52:12.953 --> 01:52:14.580
who would come to
the restaurant where she worked.


01:52:14.688 --> 01:52:16.280
- She was popular.
- Very.


01:52:16.390 --> 01:52:18.017
Yeah. So...


01:52:18.125 --> 01:52:20.059
She and her husband,
they move into their new house,


01:52:20.160 --> 01:52:21.787
and one night they throw
this painting party.


01:52:21.896 --> 01:52:22.988
And what's a painting party?


01:52:23.097 --> 01:52:25.065
It's a party where people come
and help you paint.


01:52:25.165 --> 01:52:26.257
Sounds like a terrible party.


01:52:26.367 --> 01:52:30.133
Well, supposedly,
somebody who's not Waters shows up.


01:52:30.237 --> 01:52:32.102
And Darlene is terrified of him.


01:52:32.206 --> 01:52:33.935
So you think that Darlene knew Zodiac?


01:52:34.041 --> 01:52:38.501
And if Zodiac knew Darlene,
then maybe Mageau knows Zodiac.


01:52:38.612 --> 01:52:40.443
Maybe. But Mageau's gone.


01:52:40.547 --> 01:52:42.139
So if you wanna connect
Darlene to Zodiac,


01:52:42.249 --> 01:52:43.648
you're gonna have to find another way.


01:52:43.751 --> 01:52:45.082
I have another way.


01:52:45.185 --> 01:52:46.777
Phone calls the night
of Darlene's murder.


01:52:46.887 --> 01:52:49.981
- Yeah, Zodiac called the police.
- No, Dave, there were four other calls.


01:52:50.090 --> 01:52:52.388
There were two to Darlene's house,
one to Darlene's brother-in-law,


01:52:52.493 --> 01:52:54.791
and one to Darlene's father-in-law.
Just heavy breathing.


01:52:54.895 --> 01:52:56.726
They started around 1:30 a. m.,


01:52:56.830 --> 01:53:00.493
and this was before anyone in the family
knew that Darlene had been shot.


01:53:00.601 --> 01:53:02.694
- This was in the Vallejo files?
- Yeah.


01:53:02.803 --> 01:53:03.827
God damn it.


01:53:03.938 --> 01:53:05.667
It's got to be more
than just a coincidence, right?


01:53:05.773 --> 01:53:08.640
I mean, somebody doesn't just randomly
prank phone call a victim's entire family


01:53:08.742 --> 01:53:10.767
90 minutes after they were shot.


01:53:10.878 --> 01:53:12.937
So, either Zodiac shoots
a random couple,


01:53:13.047 --> 01:53:14.537
then he recognizes Darlene...


01:53:14.648 --> 01:53:16.639
Or Darlene was shot on purpose.


01:53:16.750 --> 01:53:19.947
Either way,
Zodiac had to have known Darlene.


01:53:21.855 --> 01:53:23.584
That's good, Robert.


01:53:24.091 --> 01:53:27.288
So, I can't find Mageau,
so maybe I can find Darlene's sister.


01:53:27.394 --> 01:53:29.294
And maybe she can tell me
who this mystery man is.


01:53:29.396 --> 01:53:32.194
Try that. I've got to go. She's very cute.


01:53:36.103 --> 01:53:37.627
You know,


01:53:37.738 --> 01:53:41.071
it's interesting that you should mention
Zodiac calling people at home.


01:53:41.175 --> 01:53:42.608
He did that in San Francisco once.


01:53:42.710 --> 01:53:44.200
What? Who did he call?


01:53:44.311 --> 01:53:47.371
I can't tell you.
That's privileged information.


01:53:48.015 --> 01:53:50.176
But maybe Melvin Belli could.


01:53:52.853 --> 01:53:54.377
Melvin Belli.


01:53:55.322 --> 01:53:57.586
How do I get to Melvin Belli?


01:53:57.691 --> 01:54:00.683
- He should be along soon.
- Oh, that's all right.


01:54:00.794 --> 01:54:03.160
I've really...
I've only been waiting two hours, so...


01:54:03.263 --> 01:54:05.094
He's usually not this late.


01:54:05.199 --> 01:54:07.963
Oh, cookies. Thank you.
These look great.


01:54:08.802 --> 01:54:12.704
- You are here on business?
- I'm writing a book about the Zodiac.


01:54:12.806 --> 01:54:15.741
I remember that. I spoke to him.


01:54:15.843 --> 01:54:20.439
- You mean to Mr. Belli about the case?
- No, to the Zodiac when he called.


01:54:20.547 --> 01:54:23.846
He said he had to kill
because it was his birthday.


01:54:23.951 --> 01:54:27.182
He said it... Wait.
He said it was his birthday?


01:54:27.287 --> 01:54:29.812
Yes. You want something to drink?


01:54:30.858 --> 01:54:34.851
- When was this?
- Oh, so many years ago.


01:54:36.563 --> 01:54:39.123
Mr. Belli was away for Christmas.


01:54:39.233 --> 01:54:40.461
Gone for a week.


01:54:40.567 --> 01:54:42.899
The Zodiac called,
wanting to talk to him.


01:54:43.003 --> 01:54:44.698
I said, "He is not here. "


01:54:44.805 --> 01:54:47.706
He said, "I have to kill.
Today is my birthday. "


01:54:47.808 --> 01:54:49.742
And then he hangs up.


01:54:49.843 --> 01:54:51.333
Then the letter arrived.


01:54:51.445 --> 01:54:55.472
So, the call came
before the letter of December 20th.


01:54:55.582 --> 01:54:57.516
Mr. Belli was gone for a week?


01:54:57.618 --> 01:55:01.349
He came back on Christmas.
Not a good day to work.


01:55:01.455 --> 01:55:03.389
So, he left on the 18th.


01:55:04.591 --> 01:55:06.058
Is that helpful?


01:55:06.160 --> 01:55:07.593
She said it was his birthday.


01:55:07.694 --> 01:55:11.494
<i>Well, you'd have to confirm that,
now wouldn't you?</i>


01:55:11.598 --> 01:55:12.997
How?


01:55:13.100 --> 01:55:16.194
<i>Well, I never spoke to her,
but maybe my partner did.</i>


01:55:16.303 --> 01:55:19.136
<i>- How do I get a hold of him?
- You don't. Bill wanted out of this.</i>


01:55:19.239 --> 01:55:21.503
<i>As far as I'm concerned,
he should stay out.</i>


01:55:21.608 --> 01:55:22.870
How do I confirm it?


01:55:22.976 --> 01:55:25.501
<i>Well, if my partner
did talk to someone from Justice,</i>


01:55:25.612 --> 01:55:27.170
<i>then they would've had
to put that in a report.</i>


01:55:27.281 --> 01:55:29.579
<i>That's standard procedure.</i>


01:55:29.683 --> 01:55:31.742
<i>- Okay.
- Mel Nicolai.</i>


01:55:31.852 --> 01:55:33.786
<i>- Thank you.
- Goodbye.</i>


01:55:33.887 --> 01:55:36.048
I just need to confirm a date.


01:55:36.156 --> 01:55:37.487
- Mr. Graysmith...
- I've narrowed it down


01:55:37.591 --> 01:55:39.855
between the 18th and the 20th
of December, and I just need...


01:55:39.960 --> 01:55:43.259
Okay, I'll play.
Let's say this phone call did take place.


01:55:43.363 --> 01:55:44.796
Let's say it really was Zodiac.


01:55:44.898 --> 01:55:47.662
Why would he volunteer
the day he was born?


01:55:47.768 --> 01:55:49.895
Plus, nobody died on December 18th,


01:55:50.003 --> 01:55:52.801
just like nobody died over the weekend
when he was gonna kill a dozen people,


01:55:52.906 --> 01:55:55.238
or when he was gonna
shoot school kids or blow up buses.


01:55:55.342 --> 01:55:56.707
He's a liar, Mr. Graysmith.


01:55:56.810 --> 01:55:58.471
What if he made a mistake?


01:55:58.579 --> 01:56:00.604
What if he wasn't lying?
What if it was him on the phone?


01:56:00.714 --> 01:56:03.080
He didn't expect to pick it up,
a nice person to pick up.


01:56:03.183 --> 01:56:04.514
What if? What if? What if?


01:56:04.618 --> 01:56:07.951
Look, off the record,
Bill Armstrong checked this out.


01:56:08.055 --> 01:56:10.649
We took this very seriously.


01:56:10.757 --> 01:56:13.988
None of the suspects had the
same birthday as this phantom caller.


01:56:14.094 --> 01:56:16.255
Bill Armstrong.


01:56:21.835 --> 01:56:23.803
Can I give you a piece of advice?


01:56:23.904 --> 01:56:25.462
You're looking in the wrong place.


01:56:25.572 --> 01:56:28.598
Handwriting, fingerprints,
that's what this whole thing's about.


01:56:28.709 --> 01:56:30.074
Stick to the evidence.


01:56:31.111 --> 01:56:32.135
Hi.


01:56:40.454 --> 01:56:43.582
- Hey. How was your day?
- Long.


01:56:49.029 --> 01:56:50.428
Who's Sherwood Morrill?


01:56:50.531 --> 01:56:53.295
He's a handwriting expert
in Sacramento.


01:56:53.400 --> 01:56:54.492
He called.


01:56:54.601 --> 01:56:56.694
He said he can meet you
tomorrow morning at 7:00.


01:56:56.803 --> 01:56:58.065
Oh, great.


01:56:58.172 --> 01:57:01.005
- So you're taking off work?
- Just an hour.


01:57:02.809 --> 01:57:04.902
Sacramento's two hours away.


01:57:06.046 --> 01:57:07.638
- Really?
- Yes.


01:57:08.415 --> 01:57:09.939
What's this?


01:57:10.050 --> 01:57:12.678
Oh, that's that article.


01:57:12.786 --> 01:57:16.347
"Robert Graysmith has quietly been
shopping his book about the Zodiac. "


01:57:16.456 --> 01:57:17.548
Yeah.


01:57:17.658 --> 01:57:20.286
It talks all about you
researching Zodiac.


01:57:20.394 --> 01:57:21.793
Well, that's what the article's about.


01:57:21.895 --> 01:57:24.329
I'm not so sure that's something
we want people to know about.


01:57:24.431 --> 01:57:25.489
Why? Are you embarrassed?


01:57:25.599 --> 01:57:28.762
Robert, what's the one thing
we know about Zodiac?


01:57:29.436 --> 01:57:30.630
<i>He reads the Chronicle.</i>


01:57:30.737 --> 01:57:33.228
Yeah, but he's never
gonna read Herb Caen.


01:57:37.911 --> 01:57:40.209
<i>- Hello.
- Mr. Graysmith?</i>


01:57:40.314 --> 01:57:42.874
<i>The Robert Graysmith
mentioned in the paper today?</i>


01:57:42.983 --> 01:57:46.077
<i>- Yeah?
- I can tell you who the Zodiac is.</i>


01:57:49.890 --> 01:57:50.914
Who is this?


01:57:51.024 --> 01:57:53.151
<i>The Zodiac Killer
is obsessed with movies.</i>


01:57:53.260 --> 01:57:55.956
<i>He recorded his murders on film.</i>


01:57:56.063 --> 01:57:59.430
<i>I tried to tell the police,
but they wouldn't follow through on it.</i>


01:57:59.533 --> 01:58:02.468
<i>There's a man you need to find.
His name is Bob Vaughn.</i>


01:58:02.569 --> 01:58:05.094
<i>- Pen, pen.
- V-A-U-G-H-N.</i>


01:58:05.205 --> 01:58:07.332
<i>He's a friend of the Zodiac's.</i>


01:58:07.441 --> 01:58:09.568
<i>Mr. Vaughn does not know
his friend is a killer,</i>


01:58:09.676 --> 01:58:12.270
<i>and he is storing
some film canisters for him.</i>


01:58:12.379 --> 01:58:14.074
<i>In these canisters is the evidence.</i>


01:58:14.181 --> 01:58:17.548
Okay, yeah, friend? Who is this friend?


01:58:17.651 --> 01:58:19.278
<i>You have quite enough to get started.</i>


01:58:19.386 --> 01:58:20.944
Oh, please.


01:58:21.054 --> 01:58:24.353
<i>The Zodiac's name is Rick Marshall.</i>


01:58:28.228 --> 01:58:30.059
Your toast is burning.


01:58:31.265 --> 01:58:36.259
We choose at some point in our lives
how to physically construct each letter.


01:58:36.970 --> 01:58:39.268
Once we lock that into our brains,


01:58:39.373 --> 01:58:41.671
our handwriting may change
over the years,


01:58:41.775 --> 01:58:44.437
but the moves themselves
remain unaltered.


01:58:44.544 --> 01:58:46.034
- Understand?
- Yes.


01:58:47.547 --> 01:58:49.481
Except Zodiac's doesn't.


01:58:51.184 --> 01:58:53.118
Specifically with his "K."


01:58:54.221 --> 01:58:57.190
In his first letters,
he executed the "K" with two strokes.


01:58:57.291 --> 01:58:58.815
Later letters, he did them with three.


01:58:58.925 --> 01:59:01.086
- Why?
- We don't know.


01:59:01.194 --> 01:59:03.219
Excuse me, I've got to spray this.


01:59:03.330 --> 01:59:06.458
How many suspects
were cleared through handwriting?


01:59:06.566 --> 01:59:07.999
All of them.


01:59:08.101 --> 01:59:11.559
Also the print in the cab.
No match was ever found.


01:59:11.672 --> 01:59:15.608
Is there any way that someone
could beat a handwriting test?


01:59:15.709 --> 01:59:16.801
No.


01:59:16.910 --> 01:59:20.073
Whoever the Zodiac is,
he's not someone I cleared.


01:59:21.014 --> 01:59:24.472
About a month ago, a man showed up
on my doorstep very distraught.


01:59:24.584 --> 01:59:26.643
His name was Wallace Penny.


01:59:27.487 --> 01:59:29.751
He said he knew who the Zodiac was.


01:59:29.856 --> 01:59:31.915
Gave me a name.


01:59:32.025 --> 01:59:34.152
Rick. Rick somebody.


01:59:34.261 --> 01:59:36.695
- Rick Marshall?
- Yeah.


01:59:36.797 --> 01:59:39.322
I think that the man
who you talked to called me, too.


01:59:39.433 --> 01:59:42.027
After he left, then I checked my files.


01:59:42.135 --> 01:59:43.966
I never cleared a Rick Marshall.


01:59:51.178 --> 01:59:52.304
Hello?


01:59:57.417 --> 01:59:59.112
Hello? Who is this?


02:00:09.229 --> 02:00:10.958
It's the wrong number.


02:00:17.170 --> 02:00:20.298
Does the name Rick Marshall
mean anything to you?


02:00:21.308 --> 02:00:23.469
What are you after?


02:00:23.577 --> 02:00:24.635
What do you got?


02:00:24.745 --> 02:00:29.876
Hypothetically, you just named
my favorite suspect in the whole case.


02:00:29.983 --> 02:00:31.507
This is off the record.


02:00:31.618 --> 02:00:34.052
Couple years back,
I was trying to get Marshall's prints.


02:00:34.154 --> 02:00:35.883
I handed him a photo.


02:00:35.989 --> 02:00:38.355
He looks at it. He's about to give it back
and he stops and he says,


02:00:38.458 --> 02:00:40.892
"My goodness,
I got fingerprints all over this. "


02:00:40.994 --> 02:00:42.825
And he wipes them off.


02:00:43.430 --> 02:00:45.261
Why didn't you test him for handwriting?


02:00:45.365 --> 02:00:47.993
Because when they finally
did run his prints,


02:00:48.101 --> 02:00:50.365
they cleared him
against the one in Stine's cab.


02:00:50.470 --> 02:00:52.461
- So, then, it's not him.
- Maybe yes, maybe no.


02:00:52.572 --> 02:00:54.699
No. What do you mean?


02:00:54.808 --> 02:00:57.174
Zodiac left gloves behind at the scene.


02:00:57.277 --> 02:00:59.302
If he had the foresight
to bring gloves with him,


02:00:59.413 --> 02:01:01.404
how the hell's he gonna
accidentally leave a print behind?


02:01:01.515 --> 02:01:03.506
But it was in the victim's blood.


02:01:03.617 --> 02:01:04.948
Could have been one of the bystanders,


02:01:05.051 --> 02:01:07.417
or a cop just reaches out,
boom, false print.


02:01:07.521 --> 02:01:09.887
Yeah, but that print
disqualified 2,500 suspects.


02:01:09.990 --> 02:01:11.287
Which is why we also used handwriting.


02:01:11.391 --> 02:01:12.688
But not for Rick Marshall.


02:01:12.793 --> 02:01:15.853
SFPD saw a handwritten sign
in the window of his house.


02:01:15.962 --> 02:01:19.796
Decided it looked nothing
like the Z letters, so they just moved on.


02:01:19.900 --> 02:01:22.130
How do they know
that Rick Marshall wrote the sign?


02:01:22.235 --> 02:01:23.224
My thoughts exactly.


02:01:24.438 --> 02:01:28.169
Rick Marshall was a Navy man.
He received code training.


02:01:28.275 --> 02:01:30.709
He was also a projectionist
at a silent film theater.


02:01:30.811 --> 02:01:32.904
Well, then, how do I get copies
of Rick Marshall's handwriting?


02:01:33.013 --> 02:01:36.881
Three ways.
One, get a warrant, which you can't.


02:01:36.983 --> 02:01:39.110
Two, get him to volunteer,
which he won't.


02:01:39.219 --> 02:01:41.119
Yeah, and three?


02:01:41.221 --> 02:01:42.848
Get creative.


02:01:42.956 --> 02:01:45.686
<i>I don't know what to tell you.
You get it, I'll analyze it.</i>


02:01:45.792 --> 02:01:47.157
<i>Beyond that, you're on your own.</i>


02:01:47.260 --> 02:01:49.694
Okay, what about
the guy who came to see you,


02:01:49.796 --> 02:01:51.195
the one who called me?


02:01:51.298 --> 02:01:53.766
<i>You mean Wallace Penny?</i>


02:01:53.867 --> 02:01:55.960
Yeah. Did he leave a number?


02:02:05.312 --> 02:02:08.577
<i>- Hello?
- Hi, this is Robert Graysmith.</i>


02:02:08.682 --> 02:02:09.671
<i>How did you find me?</i>


02:02:09.783 --> 02:02:11.808
I need a sample
of Rick Marshall's handwriting.


02:02:11.918 --> 02:02:13.215
<i>I told you. Vaughn is who...</i>


02:02:13.320 --> 02:02:16.289
Mr. Penny,
if Rick Marshall is the Zodiac,


02:02:16.389 --> 02:02:18.857
I need a sample of his handwriting
to confirm it.


02:02:18.959 --> 02:02:20.551
Can you help me or not?


02:02:22.262 --> 02:02:26.926
<i>Rick used to draw movie posters
for the theater Vaughn worked at.</i>


02:02:27.033 --> 02:02:28.933
<i>- I'll send one down.
- Thank you.</i>


02:02:38.945 --> 02:02:41.345
- I'll need to see more samples.
- Yeah, but is it...


02:02:41.448 --> 02:02:43.939
It's as close as I've ever seen.
We have to tread lightly here.


02:02:44.050 --> 02:02:46.484
We're talking about
implicating this man as the Zodiac.


02:02:46.586 --> 02:02:49.578
I can get more. I'll just find Vaughn
and I'll track down Linda.


02:02:49.689 --> 02:02:51.657
I mean, Linda is Darlene's sister.


02:02:51.758 --> 02:02:54.454
I've been to the DMV,
and I talked to her parents,


02:02:54.561 --> 02:02:57.655
but still, nobody knows
where to find her.


02:02:57.764 --> 02:03:02.224
Mr. Graysmith, most of the writing
matches the exemplar.


02:03:02.335 --> 02:03:05.361
In a way, though, it's the part that
doesn't match that scares me the most.


02:03:05.472 --> 02:03:07.872
- What do you mean?
- Well, on the poster,


02:03:07.974 --> 02:03:11.068
the one letter that absolutely,
positively does not match


02:03:11.177 --> 02:03:12.735
is the letter "K."


02:03:14.748 --> 02:03:18.616
You wouldn't happen to have any
animal crackers in there, would you?


02:03:18.718 --> 02:03:22.279
<i>Unit Five.
Toschi needs to call in on a landline.</i>


02:03:34.301 --> 02:03:36.667
<i>- Dispatch.
- Hey. Dave Toschi.</i>


02:03:36.770 --> 02:03:38.362
<i>I'll connect you.</i>


02:03:39.172 --> 02:03:40.605
<i>- Dave?
- Yeah. What's up?</i>


02:03:40.707 --> 02:03:43.073
<i>Jennings here from the Chronicle.</i>


02:03:43.176 --> 02:03:45.144
It came in this morning
and you need to see it right now.


02:03:45.245 --> 02:03:46.303
See what?


02:03:46.413 --> 02:03:49.143
<i>The new Zodiac letter.
And it mentions you.</i>


02:03:49.249 --> 02:03:50.307
Okay, okay.


02:03:52.619 --> 02:03:54.883
Shit. All right, come on.


02:03:54.988 --> 02:03:56.922
Hall of Justice!


02:03:57.023 --> 02:04:00.083
Now! Come on, come on,
come on, come on, come on!


02:04:06.333 --> 02:04:07.391
Dave!


02:04:08.535 --> 02:04:10.469
Do you have it with you?


02:04:13.607 --> 02:04:16.041
"This is the Zodiac speaking.
I'm back with you.


02:04:16.142 --> 02:04:19.202
"Tell Herb Caen I am here,
I have always been here.


02:04:19.312 --> 02:04:22.338
"That city pig Toschi is good,
but I am smarter and better.


02:04:22.449 --> 02:04:25.145
"He will get tired, then leave me alone.


02:04:25.251 --> 02:04:28.709
"I'm waiting for a good movie about me.
Who will play me?


02:04:28.822 --> 02:04:30.847
"I'm now in control of all things. "


02:04:30.957 --> 02:04:33.448
These guys are from Internal Affairs.


02:04:35.395 --> 02:04:37.124
We need to talk.


02:04:37.230 --> 02:04:38.993
<i>Good evening. Our top story tonight,</i>


02:04:39.099 --> 02:04:41.590
<i>the San Francisco Police Department
has confirmed</i>


02:04:41.701 --> 02:04:44.192
<i>that the man
who calls himself the Zodiac</i>


02:04:44.304 --> 02:04:48.673
<i>and terrorized the Bay Area
has broken his silence of 51 months.</i>


02:04:48.775 --> 02:04:51.243
<i>In a letter claiming,
"I am back with you,"</i>


02:04:51.344 --> 02:04:54.802
<i>the Zodiac makes no overt threats
against the citizenry,</i>


02:04:54.914 --> 02:04:58.077
<i>and muses that his life and times
would make the best movie script yet.</i>


02:04:58.184 --> 02:04:59.674
These carrots are perfect.


02:04:59.786 --> 02:05:01.151
<i>The terse 66 word message
also manages...</i>


02:05:01.254 --> 02:05:02.278
Just go.


02:05:02.389 --> 02:05:05.358
<i>...to mention San Francisco Chronicle
columnist Herb Caen</i>


02:05:05.458 --> 02:05:08.393
<i>and the Department's own
David Toschi by name.</i>


02:05:08.495 --> 02:05:10.087
<i>- May I be excused?
- Are they targets?</i>


02:05:10.196 --> 02:05:11.185
Fine, but you have to come back


02:05:11.297 --> 02:05:12.924
and finish at least half
of what's on that plate.


02:05:13.033 --> 02:05:15.228
<i>More team coverage
on the cipher slayer's return</i>


02:05:15.335 --> 02:05:17.803
<i>begins as Alan Freeman has more.</i>


02:05:17.904 --> 02:05:19.030
<i>Thank you, Eric.</i>


02:05:19.139 --> 02:05:21.607
<i>San Francisco Chronicle columnist
Armistead Maupin says</i>


02:05:21.708 --> 02:05:24.302
<i>that he thinks not only
is this new letter a forgery,</i>


02:05:24.411 --> 02:05:26.345
<i>but it was written by the very man</i>


02:05:26.446 --> 02:05:30.075
<i>trusted to hunt down this killer,
David Toschi.</i>


02:05:30.183 --> 02:05:33.949
<i>Maupin, a very well-respected author,
has gone on record saying</i>


02:05:34.054 --> 02:05:38.650
<i>that he believes Toschi wrote the letter
to drum up publicity for himself.</i>


02:05:38.758 --> 02:05:41.818
Maupin used David
as a character in his column.


02:05:41.928 --> 02:05:43.828
David got a kick out of it


02:05:43.930 --> 02:05:45.921
and so he wrote
a couple of anonymous letters


02:05:46.032 --> 02:05:47.932
asking for the character
to be brought back.


02:05:48.034 --> 02:05:51.026
<i>It was like
writing fan mail to himself. That's all.</i>


02:05:51.137 --> 02:05:53.332
<i>But David did not write that letter.</i>


02:05:53.440 --> 02:05:56.568
No, I'm sure that he didn't.
And I'm sure that this will all blow over.


02:05:56.676 --> 02:05:58.007
<i>Blow over?</i>


02:05:58.111 --> 02:06:00.170
They kicked him out of Homicide.


02:06:00.280 --> 02:06:03.579
They made him give his handwriting
like some common criminal.


02:06:03.683 --> 02:06:06.015
<i>- May I talk to him?
- No.</i>


02:06:07.187 --> 02:06:08.347
Okay, can you just ask him


02:06:08.455 --> 02:06:10.821
if he ever investigated
a man named Rick Marshall?


02:06:10.924 --> 02:06:12.687
Is that all you can think about?


02:06:12.792 --> 02:06:16.193
Mr. Graysmith,
Maupin works at your paper. We trust...


02:06:21.901 --> 02:06:23.368
This girl, she wants music lessons?


02:06:23.470 --> 02:06:24.937
Dave! Dave!


02:06:27.273 --> 02:06:29.639
I'll catch up to you.


02:06:29.743 --> 02:06:31.938
You stop calling my house.
Do you understand me?


02:06:32.045 --> 02:06:33.740
I just need your help to find Linda.


02:06:33.847 --> 02:06:35.781
- Jesus.
- Look, two seconds.


02:06:37.817 --> 02:06:40.149
Look, we've been
running handwriting samples.


02:06:40.253 --> 02:06:42.619
- Who's we?
- Sherwood and I.


02:06:42.722 --> 02:06:43.814
Sherwood?


02:06:43.923 --> 02:06:46.016
Sherwood who was fired
from Questioned Documents?


02:06:46.126 --> 02:06:47.684
Sherwood who drinks
like Paul Avery now?


02:06:47.794 --> 02:06:50.126
- He retired.
- Is that what he told you?


02:06:50.230 --> 02:06:54.098
- What, are you saying he's wrong?
- I'm saying stop calling my house.


02:06:55.034 --> 02:06:56.695
- We ran them on Rick Marshall.
- No, Robert.


02:06:56.803 --> 02:06:58.100
No, I know you don't think it's him.


02:06:58.204 --> 02:06:59.637
I mean, no, I am not having
this conversation.


02:06:59.739 --> 02:07:02.469
But I think that Marshall knew Darlene,
and I can't talk to Mageau or Linda,


02:07:02.575 --> 02:07:03.671
so I'm gonna talk to Bob Vaughn.


02:07:03.777 --> 02:07:05.005
- Robert. Robert, stop it!
- What?


02:07:05.111 --> 02:07:07.341
Okay, the Rick Marshalls
of this world will suck you dry.


02:07:07.447 --> 02:07:08.414
They're blind alleys.


02:07:08.515 --> 02:07:10.983
But he said he wasn't gonna announce
his murders anymore, Dave.


02:07:11.084 --> 02:07:12.142
He was just gonna do them.


02:07:12.252 --> 02:07:15.187
Do you know what the chances
of us arresting someone are now?


02:07:15.288 --> 02:07:19.384
Too much time has gone by, okay?
Too much of the evidence is lost.


02:07:19.492 --> 02:07:22.484
People get old, Robert. They forget.


02:07:22.595 --> 02:07:26.895
Now, I have been a cop for 25 years.
Murder police for 12.


02:07:27.000 --> 02:07:29.298
- What do you do for a living?
- You know what I do for a living.


02:07:29.402 --> 02:07:31.632
- You're a cartoonist.
- So what are you saying?


02:07:31.738 --> 02:07:34.866
I am saying Zodiac was my job.
It is not yours.


02:07:37.877 --> 02:07:40.437
- He's still out there, Dave.
- No, Robert. I am through with this.


02:07:40.547 --> 02:07:42.412
I am through with you.


02:07:48.755 --> 02:07:51.280
What about September 26, 1970?


02:07:51.391 --> 02:07:54.918
- Okay, which one was that?
- The Lake Tahoe nurse goes missing.


02:07:57.797 --> 02:07:59.264
One day before the vernal equinox.


02:07:59.365 --> 02:08:01.162
- Dad?
- Yeah. Mark that.


02:08:01.267 --> 02:08:04.634
Got another one. June 19th, 1971.


02:08:04.737 --> 02:08:07.501
That's got to be
near the summer solstice.


02:08:10.076 --> 02:08:11.407
Oh, guys.


02:08:11.511 --> 02:08:14.537
Don't tell Mom about
our special project, okay?


02:08:15.181 --> 02:08:18.673
How come you and Mom
don't sleep in the same bed anymore?


02:08:22.188 --> 02:08:23.177
Hello.


02:08:23.289 --> 02:08:25.416
<i>Mr. Graysmith,
it's Ken Narlow from Napa.</i>


02:08:25.525 --> 02:08:29.256
Oh, Captain Narlow.
Thank you for calling me back.


02:08:29.362 --> 02:08:30.989
<i>Yeah. How can I help?</i>


02:08:31.097 --> 02:08:34.533
I called you because we've been
cross-referencing lunar cycles


02:08:34.634 --> 02:08:36.226
with the Zodiac's timeline.


02:08:36.336 --> 02:08:40.602
More often than not, each cycle
since '69 corresponds with an attack


02:08:40.707 --> 02:08:43.505
or with one of the letters,
or an unsolved homicide.


02:08:43.610 --> 02:08:46.511
<i>- Who's working with you on this?
- Some colleagues.</i>


02:08:46.613 --> 02:08:47.637
Dad?


02:08:48.648 --> 02:08:51.014
- Ken, can you hold on one second?
- Dad?


02:08:51.117 --> 02:08:53.108
- What is it?
- What's this?


02:08:57.290 --> 02:09:00.555
<i>In the decade since the Zodiac's
last cipher was received,</i>


02:09:00.660 --> 02:09:04.027
<i>every federal agency
has taken a crack at decoding it.</i>


02:09:04.130 --> 02:09:06.997
<i>But today,
where those agencies had failed,</i>


02:09:07.100 --> 02:09:09.728
<i>a cartoonist has succeeded.</i>


02:09:09.836 --> 02:09:11.360
<i>How did you do it?</i>


02:09:11.471 --> 02:09:16.875
<i>Oh, just a lot of books from the library,
and I love puzzles, so I just...</i>


02:09:18.978 --> 02:09:21.173
Yeah. The fucking library.


02:09:21.281 --> 02:09:24.409
<i>I believe that you can accomplish
anything that you put your mind...</i>


02:09:27.220 --> 02:09:30.087
That's a "J"? Okay. Honor Camp?


02:09:31.724 --> 02:09:33.351
Thank you so much.


02:09:34.994 --> 02:09:37.588
Hey, we found Linda.
She's in jail. Isn't that great?


02:09:37.697 --> 02:09:38.823
Why'd you do it?


02:09:38.932 --> 02:09:40.365
Because she'll be able to identify Rick...


02:09:40.466 --> 02:09:43.162
- What are you talking about?
- You went on TV.


02:09:43.770 --> 02:09:45.431
You put yourself out there
for him to see.


02:09:45.538 --> 02:09:47.028
Oh, hon, you're being paranoid.


02:09:47.140 --> 02:09:49.131
Then who's been calling our house
in the middle of the night


02:09:49.242 --> 02:09:50.231
at least once a week?


02:09:50.343 --> 02:09:51.503
Nobody.


02:09:53.279 --> 02:09:55.179
What's it gonna take
for you to be done with this?


02:09:55.281 --> 02:09:58.182
I can't talk about this now.
I have to go see Bob Vaughn.


02:09:58.284 --> 02:10:01.447
Well, that's too bad,
because we're gonna talk about this.


02:10:01.554 --> 02:10:03.886
And when is it gonna be finished?


02:10:03.990 --> 02:10:05.924
When you catch him?
When you arrest him?


02:10:06.025 --> 02:10:08.220
- Be serious.
- I am serious.


02:10:10.129 --> 02:10:13.621
I need to know who he is.


02:10:13.733 --> 02:10:16.861
I need to stand there,


02:10:16.970 --> 02:10:20.872
I need to look him in the eye
and I need to know that it's him.


02:10:22.675 --> 02:10:25.041
Is that more important
than your family's safety?


02:10:25.144 --> 02:10:26.611
Of course not.


02:10:28.548 --> 02:10:30.914
Why? Why do you need to do this?


02:10:32.885 --> 02:10:33.943
Why?


02:10:35.788 --> 02:10:37.915
Because nobody else will.


02:10:38.024 --> 02:10:39.958
That's not good enough.


02:10:40.059 --> 02:10:41.924
Are you done? Can I go?


02:10:57.243 --> 02:10:59.268
- Mr. Vaughn?
- Mr. Graysmith?


02:10:59.379 --> 02:11:00.403
- Yes.
- Hi.


02:11:00.513 --> 02:11:01.844
You needed to speak to me?


02:11:01.948 --> 02:11:04.348
Yes. There's a coffee shop
right on the corner.


02:11:04.450 --> 02:11:07.510
- Why don't we just go to my home?
- Oh, I don't wanna put you out.


02:11:07.620 --> 02:11:09.520
It's no trouble at all.


02:11:09.622 --> 02:11:12.090
- Where are you parked?
- Just right there.


02:11:12.191 --> 02:11:15.524
- You can follow me.
- Oh. Okay.


02:11:34.147 --> 02:11:35.705
Watch your step.


02:11:36.816 --> 02:11:38.477
Come in.


02:11:40.319 --> 02:11:43.550
- Very nice house.
- Oh, thank you.


02:11:43.656 --> 02:11:45.487
It's very rustic.


02:11:45.591 --> 02:11:48.754
- Can I take your jacket?
- No, thank you, I'm fine.


02:11:48.861 --> 02:11:50.829
Okay. This way, please.


02:11:53.466 --> 02:11:55.366
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.


02:11:55.468 --> 02:11:57.993
- How about some tea?
- Oh, no, I'm all right.


02:11:58.104 --> 02:11:59.537
- You sure?
- Yes.


02:12:00.306 --> 02:12:04.174
I wanted to ask you about a film
that the Avenue may have played


02:12:04.277 --> 02:12:06.177
while you were the organist there.


02:12:06.279 --> 02:12:08.543
<i>The Most Dangerous Game?</i>


02:12:08.648 --> 02:12:11.981
Oh, it's a classic. RKO. 1932.


02:12:12.085 --> 02:12:16.784
Fay Wray, Joel McCrea, Leslie Banks.
We've run that picture many times.


02:12:16.889 --> 02:12:18.379
In '68, '69?


02:12:20.026 --> 02:12:22.221
I'd have to check my records. Why?


02:12:22.328 --> 02:12:24.387
Do you remember the Zodiac?


02:12:26.632 --> 02:12:28.896
This is about Rick Marshall, isn't it?


02:12:29.001 --> 02:12:32.402
- He was a projectionist there, right?
- For a time, yes.


02:12:32.505 --> 02:12:36.532
But I have no occasion
to correspond with him these days.


02:12:36.642 --> 02:12:39.110
Okay. Well, there is a connection


02:12:39.212 --> 02:12:41.976
between one of the Zodiac attacks
and that film.


02:12:42.081 --> 02:12:43.810
You mean the symbol?


02:12:45.084 --> 02:12:46.278
Hold on.


02:12:46.853 --> 02:12:50.949
The Zodiac symbol on film.
It's on the countdown.


02:12:54.861 --> 02:12:57.455
It's trimmed off each reel
before it's shown,


02:12:57.563 --> 02:13:00.088
but it always arrives with it.


02:13:00.199 --> 02:13:01.564
Right there.


02:13:02.201 --> 02:13:05.864
The first time I saw it in the papers,
I thought about that.


02:13:06.739 --> 02:13:08.263
We got a tip


02:13:08.374 --> 02:13:12.333
that Rick left a film canister here
that he told you never to open.


02:13:12.445 --> 02:13:15.573
A tip about a mysterious film canister?


02:13:16.449 --> 02:13:17.780
Is it true?


02:13:19.719 --> 02:13:20.879
Yes.


02:13:21.587 --> 02:13:23.885
- Did you open it?
- No.


02:13:23.990 --> 02:13:28.256
- May I see it?
- Rick took it back in 1972.


02:13:29.996 --> 02:13:34.763
This tip is how you got it in your head
that Rick is the Zodiac?


02:13:34.867 --> 02:13:36.528
That and the poster.


02:13:36.636 --> 02:13:37.967
The poster?


02:13:39.939 --> 02:13:41.702
The poster that Rick drew.


02:13:41.807 --> 02:13:45.004
The handwriting is the closest
that we have ever come to a match.


02:13:45.111 --> 02:13:48.376
- Rick didn't draw any posters.
- No, he drew this one.


02:13:48.481 --> 02:13:51.917
Mr. Graysmith, I do the posters myself.


02:13:53.319 --> 02:13:55.150
That's my handwriting.


02:14:03.429 --> 02:14:06.296
I won't take any more of your time.


02:14:06.399 --> 02:14:11.769
Why don't I just go and find out
when we played that film?


02:14:11.871 --> 02:14:13.338
Oh, that's all right.


02:14:13.439 --> 02:14:16.840
It's not a problem.
They're just down in the basement.


02:14:18.678 --> 02:14:21.579
Not many people
have basements in California.


02:14:24.283 --> 02:14:25.341
I do.


02:14:27.553 --> 02:14:29.521
You coming, Mr. Graysmith?


02:14:40.833 --> 02:14:44.496
The original studio one-sheets,
I always kept for myself.


02:14:46.405 --> 02:14:48.930
The cheapo knock-offs
like you brought today


02:14:49.041 --> 02:14:52.169
I end up tossing into the back alley.


02:15:06.692 --> 02:15:08.182
'69.


02:15:13.899 --> 02:15:15.127
You live alone?


02:15:15.234 --> 02:15:21.002
<i>Most Dangerous Game ran in May '69.</i>


02:15:21.107 --> 02:15:23.541
So, that would be about


02:15:24.477 --> 02:15:27.742
nine weeks before
the first Zodiac letter, correct?


02:15:30.683 --> 02:15:31.741
Yeah.


02:15:36.255 --> 02:15:40.521
Do you think he saw the film
in our theater and was inspired?


02:15:46.632 --> 02:15:49.499
Are you sure
there's nobody else in the house?


02:15:51.137 --> 02:15:53.799
Would you like
to go upstairs and check?


02:15:54.540 --> 02:15:55.529
No.


02:15:58.678 --> 02:16:01.203
Thank you. Thanks for everything.


02:16:02.081 --> 02:16:03.548
You're welcome.


02:16:24.870 --> 02:16:26.235
It's locked.


02:16:37.116 --> 02:16:38.413
Thank you.


02:16:41.554 --> 02:16:43.545
Good night, Mr. Graysmith!


02:17:03.075 --> 02:17:06.738
Two killers. Got to be two killers.
One has the...


02:17:15.054 --> 02:17:16.214
Guys?


02:17:49.789 --> 02:17:51.723
You've got five minutes.


02:17:59.765 --> 02:18:00.891
Linda?


02:18:02.101 --> 02:18:03.568
Hi, I'm Robert.


02:18:07.640 --> 02:18:09.369
Did you get my note?


02:18:10.109 --> 02:18:12.077
- What's this about?
- Zodiac.


02:18:13.712 --> 02:18:14.906
Figures.


02:18:16.348 --> 02:18:18.509
- You got the look.
- What look?


02:18:19.185 --> 02:18:21.176
I didn't mean anything.


02:18:22.521 --> 02:18:24.887
Tell me about this painting party.


02:18:25.825 --> 02:18:28.419
I told the cops about that so long ago.


02:18:31.997 --> 02:18:33.931
Darlene always had
a lot of boys around,


02:18:34.033 --> 02:18:35.967
even though she was married.


02:18:36.068 --> 02:18:38.059
And this one guy was weird, though.


02:18:38.170 --> 02:18:41.503
He used to bring her presents
from Tijuana and...


02:18:42.575 --> 02:18:45.339
I don't know why
she was friends with him.


02:18:45.444 --> 02:18:47.912
She once told me he'd killed somebody.


02:18:48.013 --> 02:18:49.412
Really?


02:18:49.515 --> 02:18:51.881
Yeah, I think maybe
when he was in the service.


02:18:51.984 --> 02:18:53.952
- Navy?
- I think so.


02:18:54.053 --> 02:18:56.214
Was he into movies?
Was he a movie buff?


02:18:56.322 --> 02:18:59.223
I can tell you that
he was not into people.


02:18:59.325 --> 02:19:00.656
The party Darlene threw,


02:19:00.759 --> 02:19:03.660
people were supposed to
just show up and drink beer, help paint.


02:19:03.762 --> 02:19:05.992
But this guy showed up in a suit,


02:19:06.098 --> 02:19:09.033
and just sat in a chair
all by himself all night long.


02:19:09.134 --> 02:19:10.567
Didn't talk to anyone.


02:19:10.669 --> 02:19:12.500
And Darlene told me
to stay away from him.


02:19:12.605 --> 02:19:14.436
She was scared of him.


02:19:16.709 --> 02:19:19.177
And a couple of weeks later,
she was dead.


02:19:19.278 --> 02:19:21.746
I'm sorry. Do you remember his name?


02:19:22.748 --> 02:19:26.616
I mean, it was short,
like a nickname, like Stan.


02:19:26.719 --> 02:19:29.017
- Rick?
- No, I don't think so.


02:19:29.922 --> 02:19:32.117
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.


02:19:32.224 --> 02:19:34.749
How can you be sure?
It was a long time ago. Think hard.


02:19:34.860 --> 02:19:36.885
I am thinking hard.


02:19:36.996 --> 02:19:38.361
It was Rick.


02:19:39.398 --> 02:19:40.490
No, it wasn't.


02:19:40.599 --> 02:19:42.965
- It was Rick. It was Rick Marshall.
- No.


02:19:43.068 --> 02:19:44.763
Just say it!


02:19:44.870 --> 02:19:46.701
It wasn't Rick.


02:19:54.513 --> 02:19:55.844
It was Leigh.


02:19:59.018 --> 02:20:01.543
- Leigh?
- Yeah, Leigh.


02:20:02.888 --> 02:20:04.185
Sounds right.


02:20:09.028 --> 02:20:11.861
Officer! I need you to let me in.


02:20:11.964 --> 02:20:14.091
- Is this an emergency?
- No, I just need to see one file.


02:20:14.199 --> 02:20:15.826
No, you need to come back
tomorrow morning.


02:20:15.935 --> 02:20:18.130
- One file, just for one second.
- 8:00 a. m., when we're open.


02:20:18.237 --> 02:20:19.864
Sergeant! Sergeant Mulanax!


02:20:19.972 --> 02:20:22.406
Sergeant, I just need to see one file!


02:20:22.508 --> 02:20:25.909
Just give me five minutes.
I know exactly where it is.


02:20:26.912 --> 02:20:28.072
Please!


02:20:41.460 --> 02:20:43.121
I shouldn't be talking to you.


02:20:43.228 --> 02:20:45.219
- You got five minutes.
- Okay.


02:20:47.499 --> 02:20:48.727
Here. Here.


02:20:48.834 --> 02:20:52.600
Linda states that some of
Darlene's closest friends are Leigh,


02:20:52.705 --> 02:20:55.674
who used to bring Darlene
presents from Tijuana.


02:20:55.774 --> 02:20:57.674
- So what?
- He knew her.


02:20:57.776 --> 02:20:59.471
Linda said Leigh. This is Leigh.


02:20:59.578 --> 02:21:02.012
No. That's just one name in a file
that contains hundreds.


02:21:02.114 --> 02:21:03.547
It's nothing.


02:21:04.216 --> 02:21:06.377
- Dave Toschi...
- Agrees with me.


02:21:07.019 --> 02:21:09.886
Our investigation
into this subject is over.


02:21:12.891 --> 02:21:14.153
I'm sorry.


02:21:23.335 --> 02:21:24.461
Hello.


02:21:39.652 --> 02:21:41.051
Who's there?


02:21:44.523 --> 02:21:48.015
- You didn't return my calls.
- Oh, I've been kind of busy.


02:21:48.127 --> 02:21:49.958
Yeah. I can see that.


02:21:52.197 --> 02:21:54.028
How's the book coming?


02:21:57.102 --> 02:21:59.093
I tried to send you these.


02:22:00.205 --> 02:22:01.968
<i>I called the Chron.</i>


02:22:02.074 --> 02:22:04.838
Well, I'm not a cartoonist anymore, so...


02:22:06.412 --> 02:22:07.606
I heard.


02:22:12.785 --> 02:22:15.379
When's the last time
you ate something?


02:22:17.923 --> 02:22:20.016
Nothing makes sense anymore.


02:22:22.728 --> 02:22:24.992
- Did it ever?
- Yeah, it did.


02:22:26.498 --> 02:22:29.399
Robert, it was just the date
that didn't end.


02:22:29.902 --> 02:22:31.665
You don't mean that.


02:22:33.105 --> 02:22:34.299
A little.


02:22:37.176 --> 02:22:38.973
The kids miss you.


02:22:39.078 --> 02:22:42.172
- I can't have them see me like this.
- Neither can I.


02:22:42.948 --> 02:22:45.041
So, do whatever you have to,


02:22:46.018 --> 02:22:47.542
but finish this.


02:23:15.114 --> 02:23:16.172
Dave!


02:23:16.949 --> 02:23:18.576
Dave! It's Robert!


02:23:20.853 --> 02:23:22.480
- Dave!
- Is he actually here?


02:23:22.588 --> 02:23:24.283
I'm gonna kill him.


02:23:24.656 --> 02:23:27.250
I'm calling SFPD. Where's my gun?


02:23:29.828 --> 02:23:30.954
Dave!


02:23:31.063 --> 02:23:32.792
Robert! Go away!


02:23:32.898 --> 02:23:34.866
Dave! He made a mistake!


02:23:34.967 --> 02:23:36.935
- Get away from the window.
- I'll meet you around front.


02:23:37.035 --> 02:23:38.502
No, you won't.


02:23:39.671 --> 02:23:41.866
- You have to hear this!
- No, I don't, Robert!


02:23:41.974 --> 02:23:44.442
The birthday was the one time
that he was weak!


02:23:44.543 --> 02:23:46.340
The one time
that he gave something away!


02:23:46.445 --> 02:23:49.744
- Robert, I am calling the police.
- It's Arthur Leigh Allen!


02:23:54.787 --> 02:23:57.051
Where did you get that name?


02:23:57.156 --> 02:23:58.680
He called the Bellis' house.


02:23:58.791 --> 02:24:01.021
December '69.
"I need to kill. Today's my birthday. "


02:24:01.126 --> 02:24:03.094
It was his birthday.


02:24:03.195 --> 02:24:06.096
Arthur Leigh Allen
was born on December 18th.


02:24:09.168 --> 02:24:10.533
Get in here.


02:24:12.671 --> 02:24:14.832
- Here you go.
- Thanks.


02:24:17.810 --> 02:24:19.641
He wrote me, you know?


02:24:20.345 --> 02:24:21.471
2,500 suspects,


02:24:21.580 --> 02:24:25.016
the only one who ever wrote me
a letter was Leigh Allen.


02:24:26.084 --> 02:24:27.779
They like to help, you know, sometimes.


02:24:27.886 --> 02:24:29.319
Yes, Robert, I know.


02:24:30.789 --> 02:24:33.485
He was arrested January 1975
for molestation.


02:24:33.592 --> 02:24:35.492
He sent me that when he got out.


02:24:35.594 --> 02:24:38.324
"Dear Dave, if I can ever be
of any help to you, just let me know.


02:24:38.430 --> 02:24:40.261
"I'm sorry I wasn't your man. "


02:24:40.365 --> 02:24:41.923
And it's typewritten.


02:24:42.034 --> 02:24:44.400
Using a typewriter is not a crime.


02:24:45.871 --> 02:24:47.634
And he knew Darlene.


02:24:49.041 --> 02:24:51.032
It's in the Vallejo files.


02:24:56.248 --> 02:24:59.581
Mulanax said that
he was your favorite suspect.


02:24:59.685 --> 02:25:03.644
That you spent two years on him,
and that nobody ever came close.


02:25:06.725 --> 02:25:08.693
All the evidence said no.


02:25:09.995 --> 02:25:12.225
Sherwood disqualified his handwriting.


02:25:12.331 --> 02:25:15.459
The same Sherwood
that drinks like Paul Avery now?


02:25:16.368 --> 02:25:18.302
Yes, you have Sherwood Morrill
in writing saying,


02:25:18.403 --> 02:25:19.427
"I'm sorry, this just won't work. "


02:25:19.538 --> 02:25:21.301
- But you also have Terry Pascoe...
- His protégé.


02:25:21.406 --> 02:25:22.430
Yeah, fine, it's his protégé,


02:25:22.541 --> 02:25:24.372
but he's a handwriting expert
nonetheless, and he's saying,


02:25:24.476 --> 02:25:27.172
"Do not disqualify this suspect
on the basis of handwriting. "


02:25:27.279 --> 02:25:29.213
- So the two cancel each other out.
- No, they don't.


02:25:29.314 --> 02:25:30.611
It was Sherwood's case.


02:25:30.716 --> 02:25:32.183
He was the head
of Questioned Documents.


02:25:32.284 --> 02:25:33.615
If it went to trial,


02:25:33.719 --> 02:25:36.688
all the defense would have to do
is call Sherwood to the stand.


02:25:36.788 --> 02:25:39.416
And there was no way of getting Allen
into court in the first place,


02:25:39.524 --> 02:25:40.752
because there was no evidence, Robert.


02:25:40.859 --> 02:25:42.019
What do you mean,
there's no evidence?


02:25:42.127 --> 02:25:43.219
You have him seen with the ciphers.


02:25:43.328 --> 02:25:45.558
The military boot prints.
The same size shoes and gloves.


02:25:45.664 --> 02:25:47.859
<i>The Most Dangerous Game.
The Zodiac watch.</i>


02:25:47.966 --> 02:25:49.160
The background with school children.


02:25:49.268 --> 02:25:51.099
The misspellings of Christ-mass.
The bloody knives.


02:25:51.203 --> 02:25:53.068
All circumstantial.


02:25:53.171 --> 02:25:55.901
Paul Stine's shirt, his wallet, his keys.


02:25:56.008 --> 02:25:57.771
We should have found
one of those things in that trailer.


02:25:57.876 --> 02:25:59.571
- We didn't.
- That's...


02:26:02.014 --> 02:26:04.005
Okay. Catherine Allen states that


02:26:04.116 --> 02:26:06.243
"Leigh cleaned out his trailer
on Friday after work


02:26:06.351 --> 02:26:10.014
"and moved it to Santa Rosa
on Saturday, August 7th, 1971."


02:26:10.122 --> 02:26:12.113
You interviewed him
at the refinery on August 4th.


02:26:12.224 --> 02:26:13.748
- Yeah.
- So, he's cleaning out his trailer,


02:26:13.859 --> 02:26:17.693
he's moving into a different county
48 hours after you interviewed him?


02:26:19.298 --> 02:26:22.290
Okay. Okay.
Look at the stuff side by side, Dave.


02:26:22.401 --> 02:26:23.493
All right.


02:26:23.602 --> 02:26:26.366
Okay, Arthur Leigh Allen
and the Zodiac, their timelines.


02:26:26.471 --> 02:26:29.133
- When was the first murder in Vallejo?
- Christmas, 1968.


02:26:29.241 --> 02:26:31.835
Eight months before that,
Allen is fired for molesting his students


02:26:31.944 --> 02:26:34.037
and his family discovers
that he's a pedophile.


02:26:34.146 --> 02:26:36.444
- Now, when do the letters begin?
- July, '69.


02:26:36.548 --> 02:26:38.209
After the murder of Darlene Ferrin.


02:26:38.317 --> 02:26:41.377
And they continue
until you go to see him at work.


02:26:41.486 --> 02:26:44.717
Now, after that, do any of the letters
contain swatches of Paul Stine's shirt?


02:26:44.823 --> 02:26:46.620
No. Because he dumped them,
because he got scared.


02:26:46.725 --> 02:26:48.454
Because he knew
that you were on to him.


02:26:48.560 --> 02:26:52.291
- So, when's the next letter from Zodiac?
- Not until January of 1974.


02:26:52.397 --> 02:26:53.796
He is silent for three years.


02:26:53.899 --> 02:26:55.696
Then, in '74, he feels comfortable again


02:26:55.801 --> 02:26:57.666
because everybody's moved off
Allen as a suspect.


02:26:57.769 --> 02:26:58.758
And what do we get?


02:26:58.870 --> 02:27:02.863
Three new letters from Zodiac
in January, May, and July in '74.


02:27:02.975 --> 02:27:06.069
- But then the letters stop.
- What happens to Allen?


02:27:09.614 --> 02:27:11.081
He's arrested.


02:27:12.017 --> 02:27:15.350
January, 1975,
they send him to Atascadero.


02:27:15.454 --> 02:27:18.355
We don't get another letter from Zodiac
the entire time he's there.


02:27:18.457 --> 02:27:21.085
- When is he released?
- August, '77.


02:27:21.193 --> 02:27:24.924
Allen gets out. He types you an apology,
and then what?


02:27:25.030 --> 02:27:28.193
We get our first new Zodiac letter
in four years.


02:27:33.839 --> 02:27:37.206
Okay. Zodiac had to have known
Darlene Ferrin, right?


02:27:37.309 --> 02:27:39.539
Yes, because of the phone calls
on the night of her murder.


02:27:39.644 --> 02:27:42.442
Because of the Vallejo file,


02:27:42.547 --> 02:27:44.538
we know that Darlene knew
a man named Leigh?


02:27:44.649 --> 02:27:45.638
Yes.


02:27:45.751 --> 02:27:47.514
So, all coincidence aside, Robert,


02:27:47.619 --> 02:27:50.417
how can you be sure that Leigh Allen
is the Leigh from this file?


02:27:50.522 --> 02:27:52.990
Now, Vallejo is a small town,
but it's not that small.


02:27:53.091 --> 02:27:54.388
How do you put
the two of them together?


02:27:54.493 --> 02:27:57.656
This is a case that's covered
both Northern and Southern California,


02:27:57.763 --> 02:28:00.129
with victims and suspects
spread over hundreds of miles.


02:28:00.232 --> 02:28:01.961
- Would you agree?
- Yes.


02:28:03.235 --> 02:28:06.033
Darlene Ferrin worked
at the Vallejo House of Pancakes


02:28:06.138 --> 02:28:08.629
on the corner of Tennessee and Carol.


02:28:11.476 --> 02:28:16.209
Arthur Leigh Allen lived in his
mother's basement on Fresno Street.


02:28:17.949 --> 02:28:21.316
Door to door, that is less than 50 yards.


02:28:24.756 --> 02:28:26.223
Is that true?


02:28:27.259 --> 02:28:28.749
I've walked it.


02:28:32.597 --> 02:28:34.030
Jesus Christ.


02:28:40.739 --> 02:28:41.728
So?


02:28:45.677 --> 02:28:47.235
The prints, the handwriting...


02:28:47.345 --> 02:28:50.314
- I'm not asking you as a cop.
- But I am a cop.


02:28:53.185 --> 02:28:55.210
I can't prove this.


02:28:55.320 --> 02:28:58.255
Just because you can't prove it,
doesn't mean it's not true.


02:28:58.356 --> 02:28:59.983
Easy, Dirty Harry.


02:29:03.595 --> 02:29:05.119
Finish the book.


02:29:14.072 --> 02:29:16.506
Thank you. Thank you for breakfast.


02:30:24.809 --> 02:30:26.299
Can I help you?


02:30:27.979 --> 02:30:28.968
No.


02:31:50.161 --> 02:31:51.492
Mr. Mageau.


02:31:52.397 --> 02:31:54.695
Thanks for coming to see me.


02:31:54.799 --> 02:31:56.130
You're the one I talked to on the phone?


02:31:56.234 --> 02:31:59.761
I'm George Bawart. Vallejo PD.
I took over for Jack Mulanax.


02:32:00.805 --> 02:32:03.774
It's been 22 years.
I don't know how I can help you.


02:32:03.875 --> 02:32:05.035
Well, this is just a formality.


02:32:05.143 --> 02:32:06.542
I'm gonna show you
a group of photographs.


02:32:06.645 --> 02:32:08.510
Now, the person that shot you
may or may not be


02:32:08.613 --> 02:32:10.638
among these photographs.


02:32:10.749 --> 02:32:11.943
You don't have to pick anybody out


02:32:12.050 --> 02:32:14.211
just because I'm showing you
these pictures, you understand?


02:32:14.319 --> 02:32:15.843
Yes, sir, I do.


02:32:16.755 --> 02:32:18.086
All right.


02:32:19.124 --> 02:32:20.614
Take your time.


02:32:21.126 --> 02:32:23.924
If you don't recognize anyone,
that's okay.


02:32:35.407 --> 02:32:36.738
That's him.


02:32:38.243 --> 02:32:40.177
How sure are you?


02:32:40.278 --> 02:32:42.109
Yeah, I'm pretty sure.


02:32:44.816 --> 02:32:45.942
He had a round face like this guy.


02:32:46.051 --> 02:32:47.245
Wait. Am I to understand


02:32:47.352 --> 02:32:49.115
that you're now identifying
the second photograph?


02:32:49.220 --> 02:32:52.280
No, no. Just that
he had a round face like that.


02:32:54.359 --> 02:32:55.826
It's this man.


02:32:56.761 --> 02:32:58.058
All right.


02:32:59.898 --> 02:33:02.958
Now, on a scale of one to 10,
10 being positive,


02:33:07.072 --> 02:33:08.664
how sure are you?


02:33:12.444 --> 02:33:14.071
At least an eight.


02:33:16.881 --> 02:33:20.715
The last time I saw this face
was July 4th, 1969.


02:33:23.988 --> 02:33:26.684
I am very sure
that's the man who shot me.

